\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan snaps 6-day gaining streak on weak PMI, midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 544 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2014\par 05:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 21 (Reuters) - China's yuan snapped a six-day\par gaining streak on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a weaker\par midpoint and on further signs that recovery of the world's\par second-largest economy remains patchy. \par     The spot yuan dropped to the lowest level in a week near\par midday and is heading toward the biggest daily loss since June\par 16 when the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell 0.23 percent against the\par dollar.\par     Growth in China's vast factory sector slowed to a\par three-month low in August as output and new orders moderated, a\par preliminary private survey showed on Thursday. \par     After a hopeful bounce in June, spurred in large part by\par government stimulus, China's economic growth appears to be\par softening again, with indicators ranging from lending to output\par and investment all pointing to weakness.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the yuan midpoint at 6.1632\par per dollar prior to the market open, down 0.08 percent from the\par previous fix, marking the weakest level in two weeks.\par     The yuan opened at 6.1450 per dollar, and was changing hands\par at 6.1516 near midday, down 0.17 percent from the previous\par close.         \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                        Current    Previous     Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1632     6.158        -0.08%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1516     6.1413       -0.17%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.27%                  \par  Spot change ytd                                     -1.51%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.65%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET       \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                     Current    Difference from\par                                            onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1510     -0.11%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.233      -1.12%\par  forwards               **                 \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par