\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan snaps 5-day rising streak on weaker midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 August 2014\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan broke a five-day\par rising streak against the dollar on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official guidance rate slightly weaker than the\par previous session.\par     Still, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was hovering near five-month highs as\par investors appeared to regain a measure of confidence in China's\par economy and bet on further gains in the yuan.\par     The improving sentiment was reflected in a pick-up in long\par positions in the yuan to a near seven-month high, a Reuters poll\par showed last week.             \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1580\par per dollar prior to the market's open, weaker than Tuesday's\par fixing of 6.1548. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1436 per dollar, weaker than\par Tuesday's close of 6.1418 and was changing hands at 6.1450 in\par late morning trades.  \par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.158      6.1548    -0.05%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1449     6.1418    -0.05%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.21%               \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.48%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.69%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance: \par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1450   -0.01%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.216    -0.93%\par  forwards               **               \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange, the yuan\par is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par     For a summary of all recent coverage and graphics on the\par internationalisation of the yuan, click here: \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par  (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee; Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-8-20T03:47:39.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140820ea8k001e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
