\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises for the 5th day despite weaker fixing\b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2014\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 19 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed against\par the dollar on Tuesday for the fifth straight day despite the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  setting a lower official guidance rate.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steadied around five-month highs, as investors\par regained confidence in China's economy and bet on further gains\par in the yuan. \par     Long positions in the yuan hit a near seven-month high as\par investors piled up long positions on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid signs of\par stabilisation in the Chinese economy, a Reuters poll showed last\par week. \par     A raft of government stimulus and a long-awaited rebound in\par exports have supported manufacturing but the recovery is patchy\par and economists believe more support measures may be needed to\par counter the drag from an increasingly weak property market.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1548\par per dollar prior to market open, down 0.03 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1435 per dollar, almost flat\par from the previous close at 6.1437, and was changing hands at\par 6.1390 near midday.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:     \par  Item                       Current    Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1548     6.1528     -0.03%\par  Spot yuan                  6.139      6.1437     0.08%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.26% 