\par\par \b \uc2 China yuan's steadies at 5-month highs after stronger fix\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2014\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HONG KONG, Aug 18 (Reuters) - China's yuan held at\par five-month highs on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signaled it\par was comfortable with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent gains by setting the\par daily midpoint stronger against the dollar.\par    The yuan's recent rally has wiped out more than half of the\par 3.3 percent of losses for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this year when\par the monetary authorities engineered an unexpected depreciation \par to deter speculative bets on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's one-sided rise.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1528 \par per dollar prior to market open on Monday, slightly stronger\par than 6.1538 per dollar on Friday. The spot rate is currently\par allowed to trade 2 percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1460 per dollar, up slightly\par from 6.1470 per dollar at the previous close, and was changing\par hands at 6.1466 in late morning trades.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance:  \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1528     6.1538    0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1467     6.147     0.00%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  -0.10%               \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.51%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.65%\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1444   0.06%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2185   -1.06%\par  forwards               **               \par  * Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \u