\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan firms for 4th week, crosses 200-day moving average\b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2014\par 05:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 15 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose for the\par fourth straight week despite data that  painted a mixed picture\par of economic conditions, crossing the 200-day moving average for\par the first time since March.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.1476 per dollar at\par midday, 0.09 percent stronger than the previous close. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  (China) set the daily midpoint\par fix at 6.1538, up 0.01 percent from Thursday's fix.  \par     A slew of money and credit data published on Wednesday\par showed that China's economy is still facing downward pressure,\par despite government efforts to shore up growth. \par     Broad M2 money supply rose 13.5 percent in July from a year\par earlier, lower than the forecast 14.4 percent rise. Outstanding\par yuan loans grew 13.4 percent from a year earlier versus\par forecasts for growth of 14.0 percent. \par     However, data last week on imports and exports, which has\par the most direct impact on supply and demand in China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, showed China's export sector pushed its trade\par surplus to a record in July, fueling optimism global demand will\par help counter pressure on the domestic economy. \par     On the weekly basis, the yuan is set to rise for the fourth\par straight week around 0.05 percent. \par     The yuan's recent rally has wiped out more than half of the\par 3.3 percent of losses for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this year, when\par the monetary authorities engineered an unexpected depreciation\par of the yuan in the first four months to deter speculative bets\par on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's one-sided rise. \par     \par     LESS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BY THE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  assets owned by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  dropped again in\par July by 200 million yuan, indicating the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par reduced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market as the yuan began a\par steady rally in July. \par     However, the data released Friday morning showing that\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and commercial banks purchased 37.8 billion\par yuan worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a net basis in July, reversing\par from a negative figure in June. \par      \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                   Current         Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint          6.1538          6.1545     0.01%\par                                                    \par  Spot yuan              6.1476          6.1531     0.09%\par  Divergence from        -0.10%                     \par  midpoint*                                         \par  Spot change ytd                                   -1.52%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                34.63%\par  \par \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2090     -0.04%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2360     -1.34%\par  forwards               **               \par  \par \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.co