\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan stays flat but spot rate crosses midpoint again\b0\par\par\uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2014\par 05:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 14 (Reuters) - China's yuan stayed flat\par against the dollar on Thursday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  setting\par the official rate slightly down.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1545\par per dollar prior to market open, down 0.03 percent from the\par previous fix. \par     The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2 percent above\par or below the midpoint.\par     Spot yuan opened at 6.1538 per dollar and was changing hands\par at 6.1545 by midday, almost unchanged from the previous close.\par     The value of the spot rate crossed the midpoint, reflecting\par a previous trend of the spot market trading closely with the\par official midpoint fix.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1545     6.1533    -0.02%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1545     6.1544    0.00%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.00%                \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.64%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.48%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                           