\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan retreats from near 5-month high versus dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2014\par 06:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, Aug 12 (Reuters) - China's yuan retreated against\par the dollar on Tuesday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the official rate\par almost unchanged from previous fix, refusing to give rein to a\par spot market that a day earlier had traded the yuan at its\par strongest level since March 17.\par      \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set the midpoint rate at 6.1517\par per dollar prior to market open, up only 0.01 percent from the\par previous fix. The spot rate is currently allowed to trade 2\par percent above or below the midpoint.\par     The spot market opened at 6.1535 per dollar and was changing\par hands at 6.1566 by midday, down 0.05 percent from the previous\par close.\par     The spot rate was 0.08 percent above the midpoint, echoing a\par recent trend of the spot rate trading closely to the daily\par midpoint.\par     \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1517     6.1522    0.01%\par  Spot yuan                  6.1566     6.1536    -0.05%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.08%                \par  Spot change ytd                                 -1.67%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              34.43%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par  The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.1569   0.00%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.225    -1.18%\par  forwards               **               \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \par \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts back on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but not totally hands\par off \par     - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry trade hunters\par  \par     - China's yuan rises on dollar, pulls away from 4-1/2-month\par highs \par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.re