\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan set to fall slightly this week, underperforms midpoint\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2014\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SHANGHAI, July 11 (Reuters) - China's yuan fell against the\par dollar on Friday, with traders saying there was little evidence\par of strong dollar supply even after Beijing posted a second month\par of trade surpluses in June.\par     The yuan slipped for a second day in a row and has mostly\par underperformed the official midpoint fixing during the week.\par     Spot yuan eased to 6.2078 per dollar by midday,\par 0.08 percent weaker than Thursday's close.\par     In comparison, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 fixed its\par official midpoint at 6.1469, down 0.04 percent from\par Thursday's fixing.\par     China's trade performance improved in May and June, leaving\par a trade surplus of $31.6 billion in June alone. \par     However, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  assets, which mainly\par reflect its dollar purchases and sales on the yuan market,    \par rose a mere 361 million yuan ($58.21 million) in May, the lowest\par growth since July last year, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data published this\par week showed.\par     "The big difference between the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par asset data and the trade surplus data means banks and their\par clients are holding a large amount of dollars on hand, resulting\par in much less dollar supply of late," said a trader from a\par Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  asset data is among a slew of others that\par shows that there is now a rough balance of dollar supply and\par demand in the domestic market, enabling the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par sharply reduce the frequency of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading to\par influence the pricing of the yuan's value, traders said.\par     Echoing the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's deeds with words, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Zhou Xiaochuan\f28 \uc2 \f2  pledged on Thursday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par "significantly" reduce its yuan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when some\par prerequisites are met. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  this week fixed its midpoint generally stronger\par during the annual U.S.-China strategic and economic talks which\par ended on Thursday. But the yuan will still be down 0.06 percent\par for the week, if it closes at the midday level, traders said.\par     Traders said that the current balance of dollar supply and\par demand in the domestic market offers no favourable conditions\par for yuan appreciation for now.\par     As such, the exchange rate is likely to fluctuate around\par 6.20 within a narrow range in the near term, they said.\par            \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1469     6.1443    -0.04%\par  Spot yuan                  6.208      6.2028    -0.08%\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.99%                \par  Spot change ytd                                 -2.48%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              33.32%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan          *  6.2078   0.00%\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.259    -1.79%\par  forwards               **               \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par     FACTBOX\par     - Yuan and capital account reforms and pilot programmes     \par  \par     \par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - China's weak \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  disappoints carry traders\par  \par     - Hong Kong should cherish its standing as offshore yuan hub\par - China c.banker \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2 \par     - Dim sum bonds mark record quarter in Hong Kong\par  \par     - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par     - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields [ID:\par nL3N0KX1IA]\par \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par  \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange, the yuan\par is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par     For a summary of all recent coverage and graphics on the\par internationalisation of the yuan, click here: \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par     \par \par  (Reporting by the Shanghai Newsroom; Editing by Jacqueline\par Wong)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-11T06:24:36.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140711ea7b003xz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
