\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 2- \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  agrees to reduce  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  "as conditions permit"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,063 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2014\par 16:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reduce \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when conditions ripe\par \par \uc2 * U.S. Treasury Secretary Lew say will be watching yuan in next few months\par \par \uc2 * Both sides agree to advance on bilateral investment deal by Dec (Adds remarks from U.S. Treasury Secretary, details)\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao and Lesley Wroughton\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, July 10 (Reuters) - U.S. and Chinese leaders have agreed that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market when conditions are ripe, reaching an understanding on a prickly issue that has hurt ties between the world's two biggest economies for years.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zhou Xiaochuan said on the sidelines of annual high-level talks between the two nations that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  will "significantly" reduce its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when some prerequisites are met. He did not give further details.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said Zhou's unusual candour about \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was echoed earlier on Wednesday by the Chinese finance minister, suggested that China may be ready to let the yuan rise again once its economy stabilises.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew told reporters at the end of talks on Thursday that China was committed to reducing its interference with the yuan, "as conditions permit". China will also increase the transparency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, he said, describing the agreements as "major" changes.\par \par \uc2 "The direction of our reforms is clear: we hope that the exchange rate can be kept basically stable, at a reasonable and balanced level through reforms," Zhou said at a briefing on the sidelines of the two-day Strategic and Economic Dialogue.\par \par \uc2 "At the same time, we will allow market supply-and-demand to play a bigger role in determining the exchange rate, expand the floating range of the exchange rate, and increase the exchange rate's flexibility."\par \par \uc2 "This means that as the goals are being achieved and when conditions are ready, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will significantly reduce its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."\par \par \uc2 The value of the yuan has long strained bilateral relations between China and the United States. In June, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  judged the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be "moderately undervalued".\par \par \uc2 U.S. officials say China deliberately holds down its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost its exports, an accusation China denies.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Chinese authorities weld their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to the idea of stability, a stance that analysts say stems from China's fear of reliving Japan's experience in the 1980s, when a sharp rise in the yen hobbled the Japanese economy.\par \par \uc2 The yuan has fallen 2.4 percent so far this year as China's economic growth ground to an 18-month low in the first quarter. There are signs that activity is picking up again, though not as quickly as some had hoped.\par \par \uc2 "It feels like there was a fairly concrete discussion this time," said \uc2 Louis Kuijs\uc2 , an economist at RBS Bank in Hong Kong. "This is not just a repetition of the policy line that lay on the policy shelf.\par \par \uc2 "I think in the eyes of Beijing, once the concerns of economic growth are convincingly removed, there would be less resistance to letting the exchange rate appreciate."\par \par \uc2 WATCH THE NEXT FEW MONTHS\par \par \uc2 As had been the case in recent years, the yuan was a matter of contention at this year's Sino-U.S. talks. Lew told his counterparts from the start that a move to a market-determined exchange rate was a "crucial step" for China.\par \par \uc2 In response, Chinese Finance Minister \uc2 Lou Jiwei\uc2  said on Wednesday that Washington constantly raises the issue of whether Beijing can stop its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Lou said it was difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be hands off given its unsteady economy and abnormal capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Whether Thursday's agreement will be supported by action remains to be seen, a point noted by Lew who said he will be monitoring the renminbi's exchange rate in coming months.\par \par \uc2 "The experience of the next few months will tell us a lot about what the real impact is," he said.\par \par \uc2 Statements issued by both governments at the end of Thursday said policymakers on both sides agreed to avoid "competitive devaluation" of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  under a broader G20 deal.\par \par \uc2 The ninth-most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world, the yuan is kept on a tight leash by China compared with its peers. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sets a midpoint value every day, from which the yuan is allowed to rise or fall 2 percent in the spot market.\par \par \uc2 Before the yuan's retreat this year, \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  had denied it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly said that it had ceased its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that the yuan was near its equilibrium level, even though traders said they still saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying or selling the yuan on the market through state banks.\par \par \uc2 "China is sending a clearer message: it's unlikely for \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to completely stop (yuan) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the managed float regime," said Zhang Yongjun, a senior economist at China Centre for International Economic Exchange, a well-connected think tank in Beijing.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Zhou also signalled that it was not feasible for Chinese authorities to remain entirely on the sidelines of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "If short-term market volatility or speculative forces are too big, we should take appropriate measures," he said in reference to gyrations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Apart from the yuan, the two sides agreed to try to wrap up talks on a bilateral investment treaty by the end of the year, and begin more contentious negotiations over a "negative list" of sectors that are off-limits to U.S. investment.\par \par \uc2 Washington wants to narrow the list to open up access to more areas of China's strictly controlled economy, a process it argues will help drive China's economic reforms.\par \par \uc2 China acceded as well to allowing U.S. firms that are being investigated by its anti-trust regulators to contest evidence presented against them by Chinese agencies.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. business community had pushed Washington to add China's antitrust regime to the agenda, as companies had privately voiced concerns that Beijing was using its anti-monopoly law to drive industrial policy. (Additional reporting by Michael Martina; Writing by Koh Gui Qing; Editing by \uc2 Jacqueline Wong\uc2  and Catherine Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-10T15:31:44.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140710ea7a00152\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
