\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ.com What's News - Worldwide News Briefs For Jul 10\b0\par\par\uc2 843 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2014\par 16:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA BUDGET FOCUSES ON JOBS, GROWTH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's new government said it would overhaul extensive subsidy programs for the poor and roll out a series of more business-friendly measures in an effort to create jobs and boost economic growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEW: CHINA TO BOOST \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREIGN-EXCHANGE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TRANSPARENCY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jacob Lew said after talks in Beijing that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was committed to reducing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and was preparing to make its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more transparent. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA ELECTION RESULT IN LIMBO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The outcome of Indonesia's presidential election will remain in doubt for at least 10 days as election officials take on the laborious task of hand-counting the more than 130 million votes cast across the vast island nation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU COURT: 'LEGAL HIGHS' AREN'T MEDICINE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The EU's top court has ruled that mixtures of herbs containing synthetic cannabinoids, known as "legal highs," have no medicinal benefits. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S SENATE BLOCKS CARBON-TAX REPEAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's newly elected Senate has frustrated Prime Minister Tony Abbott's attempt to hastily scrap an unpopular tax on carbon emissions. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU COURT OVERTURNS GERMAN LANGUAGE TESTS FOR TURKS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Germany can't require the spouses of Turkish immigrants to show a basic knowledge of the German language before granting them visas, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 's top court ruled. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. TO FAST-TRACK SURVEILLANCE BILL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Legislation is required to ensure law enforcement and intelligence agencies retain existing communications surveillance capabilities, U.K. Prime Minister David Cameron and his deputy said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA EXPORTS UP ON U.S. DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese exports grew in June on the back of strengthening U.S. consumer demand, in a positive sign for China's factory sector and for the global economic outlook. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SAUDIS URGE TRIBES TO REJECT IRAQ MILITANTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Saudi Arabia is privately encouraging its allied tribes in Iraq to turn against a Sunni extremist insurgency, a pivot that could help calm sectarian tensions that underpin the uprising. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DRAGHI CALLS FOR REFORM RULES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Mario Draghi on Wednesday called for new rules on economic reforms that the countries in the euro zone should adopt to narrow their economic differences. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE KEEPS RATES UNCHANGED \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of England left the U.K.'s benchmark interest rate unchanged amid criticism that officials are sending confusing signals on when borrowing costs will eventually start to rise. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SWEDEN TO URGE MORTGAGE REPAYMENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sweden's regulations on property loans allow most borrowers to pay only interest for prolonged periods. But now the government is worried about buildup of excessive debt. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ WARNED U.N. OF STOLEN NUCLEAR MATERIAL, AGENCY SAYS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Atomic Energy Agency\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday it is aware of a letter Iraq sent to the United Nations saying militants seized nuclear material from a university in the north of the country. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ LEADER: KURDS AIDING SUNNI EXTREMISTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iraq's leader accused the country's Kurds of letting radical Islamist militants use their regional capital of Erbil as an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  center, an allegation Kurdish officials dismissed. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FINANCE MINISTER SAYS GDP TARGET NOT A 'FLOOR' \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese Finance Minister Lou Jiwei said that the government's 7.5% economic growth target isn't a "floor," suggesting that Beijing may be comfortable with slower growth. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OPEC SEES RISING GLOBAL OIL DEMAND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rising U.S. oil consumption will reverse a four-year demand decline in rich nations and drive a pick up world-wide next year, OPEC said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TYPHOON NEOGURI HEADS TOWARD TOKYO \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Typhoon Neoguri sweeps along Japan's eastern coast toward Tokyo after making landfall on the nation's southernmost main island of Kyushu. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DIPLOMATS SAY STAFFAN DE MISTURA IS NEW SYRIA ENVOY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Veteran Italian-Swedish diplomat Staffan de Mistura has been chosen by Secretary-General Ban Ki-moon to replace Lakhdar Brahimi as the international point man on Syria, U.N. diplomats said Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par APPROVAL FOR PLAN TO LIBERALIZE GREEK POWER MARKET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Greece's Parliament narrowly approved plans to eventually sell part of the state-controlled power company to private interests. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EU, GERMANY STRIKE ENERGY DEAL \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it had secured a deal with Germany to allow the country to forge ahead with its ambitious renewable-energy laws, having agreed to some key changes to the legislation. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNOWDEN SEEKS TO EXTEND STAY IN RUSSIA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Edward Snowden has asked Russian authorities to extend his stay in the country as his current residence permit is expiring. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF CHINA ACCUSED OF MONEY LAUNDERING BY STATE BROADCASTER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's state broadcaster took aim at Bank of China as it accused the lender of laundering money and helping clients skirt the country's controls on cross-border fund transfers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MYANMAR JOURNALISTS SENTENCED TO HARD LABOR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Four Myanmar journalists and the chief executive of their newspaper were sentenced to a decade in prison for publishing an article claiming that a military facility was producing chemical weapons.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (For continuously updated news from the Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 10, 2014 10:00 ET (14:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140710ea7a002ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
