\par\par \b \uc2 China Shares End Flat, Weaker-Than-Expected Trade Data Weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung   \par \uc2 461 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2014\par 10:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI--China's shares ended largely unchanged Thursday as bargain hunting in some blue chips helped to offset weaker-than-expected June trade data.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Shanghai Composite Index, which tracks both A and B shares, ended down 0.01%, or 1.57 points at 1100.86. The Shenzhen Composite Index fell 0.1%, or 1.57 points to 1100.86.\par \par \uc2 The Shanghai index is likely to remain in rangebound trading between 2000 and 2100 ahead of the release of the second-quarter GDP growth figures due Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are waiting for the positives from economic and financial reforms to trickle down to the physical market, but the targeted measures announced so far will take time before one can see any fruit," said Deng Wenyuan, an analyst at \uc2 Soochow Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 China's exports in June rose at a weaker-than-expected 7.2% year-on-year, while imports increased by 5.5% against expectations of a 5.4% rise, according to data from the General Administration of Customs.\par \par \uc2 The health of the domestic economy and pace of economic restructuring typically overshadow market news abroad, analysts say, though to a certain degree, there is also some caution about continued dearth of capital inflows, after the U.S. Federal Reserve signaled that it would end its bond buying policies in October if U.S. economic growth continues at its current pace.\par \par \uc2 Some property developers rose on bargain hunting. \uc2 China Vanke Co\uc2 ., the world's largest residential property developer by revenue, rose 1.5% to CNY8.69, after falling 2.3% over the past two sessions. \uc2 Gemdale Corp\uc2  climbed 1.2% to CNY9.52 after falling 0.3% over the same period.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the ongoing annual meeting of senior U.S. and Chinese officials called the Strategic and Economic Dialogue in Beijing so far have yielded little market moving cues, with policymakers reiterating previously announced reform moves.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zhou Xiaochuan repeated the country's intention to liberalize interest rates within two years but offered few details on the exact timing. Mr. Zhou also added that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't ready to give up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  underperformed other banks, after the country's state broadcaster accused the lender of laundering money and helping clients skirt the country's controls on cross border fund deals.\par \par \uc2 Bank of China fell 0.8% to CNY2.54.\par \par \uc2 Insurers also declined. China Pacific Insurance Group slid 1.2% to CNY17.70 and \uc2 Ping An Insurance\uc2  Group Co. of China fell 0.8% to CNY39.40.\par \par \uc2 Write to Esther Fung at esther.fung@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 July 10, 2014 04:22 ET (08:22 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140710ea7a00115\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
