\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 3-China frees retail yuan exchange rate in move toward convertibility\b0\par\par\uc2 932 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2014\par 07:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * China allows banks to freely set OTC yuan/dollar rates\par \par \uc2 * Sign that Beijing is confident yuan is reaching equilibrium\par \par \uc2 * Retail demand will influence main interbank rates\par \par \uc2 * Corporate clients will have better choices to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Repeats to fix formatting, adds details, quotes, analysis)\par \par \uc2 By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par \par \uc2 SHANGHAI/BEIJING, July 3 (Reuters) - China has permitted banks to freely set their own exchange rates for the yuan against the dollar in over-the-counter transactions -- another step toward freeing the exchange rate from government control.\par \par \uc2 Banks were previously required to price the yuan/dollar rate they offered retail clients within 3 percent in either direction of the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's midpoint on a given day.\par \par \uc2 "The liberalisation of the retail market implies that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  believes that the yuan has now reached equilibrium," said analyst Cao Yang at \uc2 Shanghai Pudong Development Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Such equilibrium permits the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gradually free the yuan's exchange rate without worrying about excessive volatility, he said.\par \par \uc2 The new rules do not apply to the yuan/dollar's main rate in the interbank market, which is subject to controls including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting a daily midpoint from which the spot rate has been allowed to fluctuate in either direction by 2 percent since March.\par \par \uc2 Under the new policy, effective immediately, banks can price OTC yuan/dollar exchange rates "in line with market supply and demand and without any restrictions", the \uc2 People's Bank of China (PBOC) \uc2 said in a statement published late on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The move "is aimed at further perfecting the mechanisms to establish market-oriented exchange rate for the yuan," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the statement.\par \par \uc2 However, the wholesale market that the banks trade in must still abide by the midpoint guidance rate. Because that primary market is an enormous source of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  supply and demand, posting around $15 billion in transactions every day, it will continue to exercise a strong influence on the retail market.\par \par \uc2 The world's second-largest economy is seeking to increase the use of the yuan in global trade and investment to diminish China's dependence on the U.S. dollar, and by extension its exposure to economic policy decisions made in Washington outside of its control.\par \par \uc2 Allowing the market to price the yuan against the dollar is a pre-requisite for wider liberalisation, and at the same time decreases the need for Beijing to accrue dollar reserves in the name of managing the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  has purposefully guided the yuan to stage more two-way trading over the past couple of years, letting the yuan appreciate 2.9 percent versus the dollar in 2013, only to push it down as much as 3.4 percent this year to convince the market not to consider the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a one-way bet on appreciation.\par \par \uc2 TESTING THE WATERS\par \par \uc2 With the first market-oriented yuan/dollar exchange rates in the OTC market, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can collect data on dollar supply and demand from major state banks, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "Retailing is also an important indicator for yuan/dollar demand and supply and reflects sentiment towards these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a senior dealer at a major European bank in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 "As such, the OTC exchange rates will have influence on the interbank rates and help banks discover market-oriented rates."\par \par \uc2 Chinese companies, which obtain foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  both at the interbank market and with a less degree, via banks' OTC channels, welcomed the move.\par \par \uc2 "The opening will have a positive impact on corporate \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals," said Wang Xinjiu, Securities Affairs Representative at \uc2 China International Marine Containers\uc2  (Group) Co , the world's top container producer.\par \par \uc2 "Companies, just like individuals, will have better channels to meet their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand with more reasonable exchange rates," he said.\par \par \uc2 The latest reform step comes ahead of bilateral economic talks between the United States and China later this month, during which U.S. officials are expected to raise their concerns about Beijing's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Critics say \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  artificially suppresses the value of the yuan to protect its exporters, an accusation China has always denied.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew, who will attend the Strategic & Economic Dialogue in Beijing later this month, said on Tuesday the yuan's value is a "very big issue" for the United States and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs to appreciate more.\par \par \uc2 Robert Minikin, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  in Hong Kong, said he believed that Beijing is also preparing to change the way it manages the market in general, and that the freeing of the retail market could be a step in this direction.\par \par \uc2 "There are some hints that the \uc2 PBOC\uc2  is changing the way it is managing the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and in particular the way the daily fix is managed. We may be moving toward a more market-driven daily fix rather than one set by the authorities."\par \par \uc2 Minikin was referring to a common complaint by participants in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, namely that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used the daily midpoint fixing as a leash to control market movements instead of an indicator of consensus price.\par \par \uc2 Economists have pointed out that so long as Beijing continues to set an official midpoint rate, it retains a tool for controlling the exchange rate; and so long as the interbank market is restrained by a trading band, the market is not truly in charge. (Additional reporting by China economics team; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-3T06:12:42.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140703ea73000h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
