\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  as deals,  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  optimism spur Hong Kong dollar gains\b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2014\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * HKMA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time in nearly 2 years\par \par \uc2 * Second busiest month for IPO markets this year\par \par \uc2 * Strong \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  turnover on Hong Kong dollar\par \par \uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 2 (Reuters) - Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg for the first time in nearly two years as investor expectations for a rebound in Chinese equities boosted the local dollar.\par \par \uc2 More capital market activity from new listings and mergers and acquisitions also triggered unusual strength in the Hong Kong dollar, which tested the strong end of its trading band, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) bought a total of $2.1 billion in the past two days to restrain gains in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is pegged to the U.S. dollar. That was the first time it did so since the fourth quarter of 2012, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Strength in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen to be triggered by speculation over a revaluation of the peg, but rather signalled cautious optimism over the outlook for Chinese equities and the completion of recent capital market deals, traders said.\par \par \uc2 "If markets were expecting a peg move, we would have seen wholesale buying of the local dollar across the board on cash and forwards and given the current situation that is unlikely the case," said the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a big Chinese bank in Hong Kong, referring to the big political protests on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.8 to the U.S. dollar, but can trade between 7.75 and 7.85. Under the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg, the HKMA is obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the Hong Kong dollar hits 7.75 or 7.85 to keep the band intact.\par \par \uc2 The HKMA, the territory's de-facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the recent strength of the Hong Kong dollar reflected "increased corporate demand due to commercial activities, including merger and acquisition activities and dividend distribution."\par \par \uc2 Turnover is brisk. Daily trading volumes in the Hong Kong dollar are a few hundred times the average volume over the last one month, Thomson Reuters data show, and at odds with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  where volumes have are more subdued.\par \par \uc2 STRENGTH SEEN SHORT-LIVED\par \par \uc2 Traders say the Hong Kong dollar's rise is in lockstep with its decline in the forwards market indicating the local dollar's strength is of a short-term nature and arising out of the short-term financing needs from banks and companies.\par \par \uc2 As the Hong Kong dollar hit the strong end of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading band, the forwards market was pricing in near-term weakness in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with 1-month, 6-month, and 12-month forwards declining in value.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  options where many hedge funds typically bet on the direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also lacklustre, a sign that local dollar strength was short-term in nature.\par \par \uc2 One-month USD/HKD 25-delta risk reversals, which indicate the extent of the bets on the local dollar, has been steady for a while implied volatility subdued\par \par \uc2 That trend is line with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Korean won and Taiwan dollar where authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  sporadically because of a soft dollar.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, investors are returning to the equities market and underpinning the Hong Kong dollar. The local stock index has turned conclusively positive for the first time this year.\par \par \uc2 Primary market activity has also picked up. June was the second-highest month for IPOs in Hong Kong this year at $3.2 billion, according to Thomson Reuters data.\par \par \uc2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp Ltd\uc2  (OCBC) said all the pre-conditions to an agreement to buy Hong Kong's \uc2 Wing Hang Bank Ltd\uc2  had been satisfied, as various regulators had given their blessing to the $4.95 billion deal.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Michelle Chen and Denny Thomas; Editing by \uc2 Jacqueline Wong\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-2T07:24:58.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140702ea72003ck\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
