\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China's rapidly rising  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves create policy difficulties - SAFE\b0\par\par\uc2 363 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2014\par 06:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Reserves can spur inflation pressures, economist says\par \par \uc2 * Regulator reiterates some reserves will be for outbound investment\par \par \uc2 * Reserves hit record $3.95 trillion in Q1 (Adds quotes from SAFE, background)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, June 12 (Reuters) - China's rapid accumulation of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves creates difficulties for steering economic policy, officials with the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 China will keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at a reasonable level, officials of the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (SAFE) said in a webcast.\par \par \uc2 "The excessively large \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves increase domestic money supply and create potential domestic inflation pressures," said Huang Guobo, chief economist of the SAFE.\par \par \uc2 "They also put more pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise reserve requirement ratios and sterilise (inflows)," he said.\par \par \uc2 Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves account for more than 80 percent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's assets, leading to a mismatch between its assets and liabilities, fuelling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks, Huang said.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's largest, grew by $130 billion in the first quarter, reaching a record $3.95 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Premier \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2  said in May that China's war chest of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had become a headache as its continued rise could stoke inflation in the long term.\par \par \uc2 Large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap rises in the yuan, amount to creation of base money and can fuel inflation unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soaks up the excess yuan injected into the system.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulator reiterated its plans to use some of the reserves for outbound investment and to improve the way it manages the reserves.\par \par \uc2 China will step up efforts to ward off economic risks to two-way capital flows, while improving the yuan regime to make it more responsive to market forces, SAFE said.\par \par \uc2 Yi Gang\uc2 , vice \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said in November that the cost of holding the reserves would surpass earnings from them when reserves exceed a certain level. (Reporting by China economics team; Editing by Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-6-15T04:33:57.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140612ea6c0035x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
