\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan edges up on \uc2 PBOC\uc2  guidance\b0\par\par\uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2014\par 06:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets midpoint stronger, guides yuan up 0.01 pct\par     * No \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as dollar supply/demand balanced -\par traders\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's foreign trade in difficulty - commerce ministry\par official\par     * Yuan seen moving narrowly throughout Q2\par \par     By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par     SHANGHAI, May 20 (Reuters) - China's yuan edged higher\par against the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set a\par slightly firmer midpoint, signalling its intention to keep the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable for now, traders said.\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.2370 per dollar by midday,\par up 0.01 percent from Monday's close, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of\par China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 set its official midpoint at 6.1626, or 0.02\par percent stronger than Monday.\par     Traders reported a rough balance of dollar supply and demand\par in the domestic market, with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  staying on the sidelines\par as the yuan remained stable.\par     The Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was seen having limited room to weaken\par further, as it did earlier this year, but also little leeway for\par gains in the near term, partly due to China's weak trade\par outlook.\par     A senior commerce ministry official said on Tuesday that  \par China faced an arduous task achieving its 7.5 percent trade\par growth target this year as the high growth period was over.\par     Zhang Ji, head of the foreign trade department at the\par Ministry of Commerce, told a news conference that violence\par against Chinese firms in Vietnam could also hurt bilateral\par trade. \par     Last week, China's cabinet announced a raft of measures to\par support the wobbly trade sector, including giving more tax\par breaks, credit insurance and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging options to its\par exporters. \par     The yuan has rebounded 0.3 percent against the dollar so far\par in May after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  engineered a 3.3 percent\par depreciation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the first four months of this\par year to deter speculators from betting on a non-stop yuan rise.\par     Before this year's unexpected depreciation, the yuan had\par steadily appreciated by more than 30 percent since its landmark\par revaluation in 2005. Many market participants believe the\par redback is close to its equilibrium level while two-way\par fluctuations will be the new norm. \par             \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1626     6.1636      0.02\par  Spot yuan                  6.2370     6.2374      0.01\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.21                 \par  (pct)                                           \par  Spot change ytd                                 -2.94\par  Spot change since 2005                          32.70\par  revaluation                                     \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par                                          (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan             6.2361   0.01\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2390   -1.22\par  forwards                                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - China seen able to tell U.S. that yuan is near fair value\par  \par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2   \par     - Dim sum bonds mark record quarter in Hong Kong\par  \par     - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par     - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://lin