\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported; MYR, PHP, INR Top Gainers -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2014\par 02:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2200-6.2416   6.2000-6.2500 \par USD/TWD   30.180-30.230   30.130-30.280 \par USD/KRW    1,027-1,030     1,020-1,033 \par USD/SGD   1.2494-1.2511   1.2450-1.2528 \par USD/MYR   3.200-3.2340    3.1880-3.2450 \par USD/THB    32.37-32.50     32.24-32.54 \par USD/PHP    43.50-43.80     44.32-43.97 \par USD/IDR   11,410-11,470   11,360-11,500 \par USD/INR    59.15-59.76     59.00-60.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation. The daily PBOC USD/CNY benchmark rate is likely to subside due to the easing of the U.S. dollar index overnight. Spot USD/CNY could hence consolidate with a slight downside bias. Volatility has ebbed recently in the spot USD/CNY market, although it could soon pick up again, based on the strong buying seen by traders late Wednesday in the offshore USD/CNH forwards market. The main theme for the yuan in the near-term remains the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to introduce more two-way volatility for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2200 (psychological support), before 6.2000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 6.2416 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.2500 (psychological resistance), before 6.2805 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD may consolidate within a narrow band of 30.180-30.230 demarcated by the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line above. The U.S. dollar treaded water overnight, providing no clues for USD/TWD direction. The pricing of the most-commonly traded 1-month nondeliverable forward contract in the offshore market suggests a neutral stance towards the Taiwan dollar. In the background, as the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield remains subdued, the greenback seems unlikely to rally. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.180 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.130 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.230 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.280 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.330 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW has lost its bearish technical bias and may consolidate slightly higher toward the psychological resistance at 1,030 instead. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  on Wednesday has signalled to speculators that the won has risen too fast in recent weeks. Traders will now be wary if USD/KRW again approaches the 1,020-1,022 level which is where the BOK was suspected to have started buying dollars aggressively late Wednesday. Trimming of short USD/KRW positions from here on may fuel the greenback higher, possibly to the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance at 1,033. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,027 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,022 (suspected BOK \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 1,020 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier ), before 1,033 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is likely caught between the upper and lower Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1), lacking a trigger for increased volatility. The intraday consolidation range spanning 1.2494-1.2554 may however be susceptible to a downside break because the USD/SGD weekly chart is looking bearish. On the weekly chart, USD/SGD is beneath the Ichimoku Cloud support zone and also within the Bollinger downtrend channel, suggesting more weakness ahead for the U.S. unit. Singapore retail sales data for March will be published at 0500 GMT. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2494 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2450 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2511 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 1.2528 (top of weekly Ichimoku Cloud and top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2554 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. The Malaysian ringgit continues to look attractive based on fundamentals and technical indicators. After the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hinted at raising interest rates last week, the ringgit has been gaining versus the U.S. dollar. On the daily USD/MYR chart, the bearish outlook indicated by the Bollinger downtrend channel suggests the ringgit could carry on appreciating toward the round-figure trading barrier at 3.2000--which may support the dollar in the interim. USD/MYR needs to stay below 3.2340 by the end of the day to maintain its bearish technical bias. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2000 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 3.1880 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is at 3.2340 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.2450 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 3.2500 (20-day Bollinger mid and psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. The Thai baht's recovery on Wednesday brought USD/THB back down into the technical consolidation zone of the daily Ichimoku Cloud spanning 32.33-32.54. The baht has recouped losses sustained last week when the Constitutional Court ruled that caretaker prime minister Yingluck Shinawatra had to step down immediately. While the political impasse drags on, the lack of protest-related violence that some had expected is helping the baht to stabilize. Unless USD/THB climbs back above the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, the baht is not as likely to weaken for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.37 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 32.33 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 32.24 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.50 (psychological resistance and daily Bollinger uptrend channel), 32.54 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 32.61 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP continues to look bearish on the daily chart, helped by improving sentiment for the peso after the S&P credit rating upgrade and liquidity-tightening steps taken by the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. The peso, which ended Wednesday at 43.55 to the U.S. unit, could be targeting the 43.32 weekly Ichimoku Cloud support. Investors turned bullish on the peso after credit ratings agency S&P raised the Philippines one notch to BBB. The credit upgrade followed the \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's anti-inflationary measure of raising its Reserve Requirement Ratio by one percentage point to limit bank lending. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 43.50 (psychological support), before 43.32 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud support). Immediate resistance is likely at 43.80 (psychological resistance), then at 43.97 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR is likely to slip toward the 11,410 base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support, which is also the base of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. The rupiah is likely to add on to Wednesday's 0.8% rise against the greenback as the market becomes more optimistic for the coalition led by the PDI-P--the party fronted by presidential hopeful Joko Widowo--and backed by Golkar, the second-largest political party. The 4-party coalition, which claimed about half the legislative seats in the April vote, has a clear chance at victory in the presidential elections scheduled July 9. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,410 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 11,360 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 11,200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 11,470 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,525 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR may drop further to 59.15, implying a stronger Indian rupee versus the U.S. unit, as investor confidence rises due to exit polls indicating a likely win for the corruption-fighting BJP party. The official election results will be announced on May 16. Indian stocks and the rupee have been enjoying an election euphoria boost as investors bet on an improvement in business conditions--though some analysts say that those expecting major changes are too optimistic. On both daily and weekly charts, USD/INR will maintain its bearish technical bias as long as the immediate technical resistance at 59.76 is unbroken. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.15 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 59.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 58.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 59.76 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 60.14 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 14, 2014 20:50 ET (00:50 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140515ea5f0006d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
