\par\par \b \uc2 China's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves may stoke inflation, a "big burden" -premier\b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2014\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BEIJING, May 11 (Reuters) - China's war chest of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves has become a headache as its continued rise could stoke inflation in the long term, Premier Li Keqiang said in remarks seen on Sunday, pledging to reduce the country's trade surplus.\par \par \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, the world's largest, grew by $130 billion in the first quarter, to a record $3.95 trillion.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at reasonable levels, partly by reducing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 "Frankly speaking, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have become a big burden for us, because such reserves translate into the base money, which could affect inflation," Phoenix New Media Ltd quoted Li as saying during a visit to Kenya.\par \par \uc2 "From China's perspective, macroeconomic controls could face tremendous pressures if the overall trade is imbalanced."\par \par \uc2 China will take steps to reduce its trade surpluses with the rest of the world, including Kenya, Li was quoted as saying.\par \par \uc2 Large foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yuan rises, amount to creation of base money and can fuel inflation unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soaks up the excess yuan injected into the system.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been suspected of engineering a fall in the yuan in a bid to punish speculators betting on yuan rises.\par \par \uc2 Yi Gang, vice \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, said in November that the cost of holding the reserves would surpass earnings from them when reserves exceed a certain level.\par \par \uc2 China's inflation has been benign in recent months as its economy slows, but analysts point to long-term pressures as the government loosens its grip on utility and resources prices. (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Clarence Fernandez)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-14T09:37:44.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140511ea5b00691\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
