\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan hits 3-week high as depreciation trend loses steam\b0\par\par\uc2 972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2014\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan gains for third straight day to 6.2226/dlr\par     * Yuan on course for strongest weekly gain since Dec 2011\par     * C.bank seen shifting course after 4-month weakening\par     * Authorities want to enforce two-way flexibility\par \par     By Gabriel Wildau\par     SHANGHAI, May 7 (Reuters) - China's yuan rose to three-week\par highs on Wednesday as traders questioned whether a third day of\par gains was a signal the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had switched its stance to\par gently supporting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after aggressively driving it\par lower this year.\par     Spot yuan changed hands at 6.2245 per dollar at\par midday on Wednesday, 0.02 percent higher than Tuesday's close.\par Earlier, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had set its daily midpoint for the\par yuan 0.04 percent stronger, the biggest gain in the midpoint in\par four weeks. \par     That took gains this week to 0.6 percent. While small by the\par standards of freely floating \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it would equal the\par largest weekly gain for the tightly managed yuan since December\par 2011.\par     Traders have said that after pushing the yuan down in recent\par months, they think the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 is now\par gently \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb expectations of further losses.\par     "While it's clearly too early to tell if the there has been\par a definitive shift in terms of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  bias around USD/CNY, the\par near-term risks suggest a continuation of this recent trend of\par CNY strength," Jonathan Cavenagh, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Westpac\par Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore, wrote in a note on Tuesday. \par     At the same time, some seasonal factors are helping, traders\par said. Yuan purchases are traditionally stronger at the start of\par each month, due to both corporate demand and position\par adjustments by dealers, and the U.S. dollar is broadly weaker.  \par     The yuan had fallen in each of first four months of 2014,\par and the cumulative loss of 3.3 percent more than reversed its\par gains of last year. It was the yuan's most sustained\par depreciation since its de-pegging from the dollar in 2005.\par     Traders and analysts widely believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par engineered the weakness in a bid to punish speculators who\par regarded yuan appreciation as a sure bet.\par     \par     TWO-WAY TRADE \par     "I can say with near certainty that the renminbi's\par depreciation in the first quarter was mainly the result of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," Yu\par Yongding, a former member of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's monetary policy committee\par told state media in an interview, using the official name for\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Yu, who is now a member of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese Academy of Social\par Sciences\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said it was "difficult to imagine" the yuan would fall\par more than 3 percent even as China's current and capital accounts\par were both in surplus during the period. \par     Market observers believe authorities are not aiming to move\par the yuan strongly in one direction or the other, but instead\par want to create the expectation of two-way trade as a way of\par discouraging excessive speculation. \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  pledged on Tuesday to keep the yuan basically\par stable while pushing reforms to help introduce greater two-way\par flexibility in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     One risk for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was that if expectations of\par further losses became entrenched, it could lead to capital\par flight and affect domestic funding conditions. \par     "Overly fast depreciation is definitely something\par (authorities) don't want to see. In the medium term, I expect\par the yuan could fluctuate in the 6.20 to 6.26 range," said a\par trader at a mid-sized Chinese bank in Beijing.\par     In an opinion column published in state media on Tuesday, a\par senior official at China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regulator criticised\par Chinese companies for being poorly prepared to handle increased\par yuan volatility. \par     In March, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  doubled the yuan's daily trading band\par from 1 percent to 2 percent on either side of the central parity\par rate that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  publishes each morning.\par \par The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1542     6.1565      +0.04\par  Spot yuan                  6.2245     6.2257      +0.02\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.11                 \par  (pct)                                           \par  Spot change ytd                                 -2.71\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation              +33.01\par  *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 2 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par     OFFSHORE CNH MARKET   \par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par                                          (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan         *   6.2266     -0.04\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2150   -0.98\par  forwards              **                \par  \par \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2   \par     - Dim sum bonds mark record quarter in Hong Kong\par  \par     - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par     - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par \par         \par     KEY GRAPHICS \par     - China hot money inflows moderate in early 2014 \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/raz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/raz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - The yuan trades weaker than fix, tests wider trading band\par \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Chinese corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior still reflects appreciation\par expectations \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/syx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/syx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's exports, imports, and trade surpluses GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   \par \par \par  (Additional reporting by Li Ran in Beijing; Editing by John\par Mair)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-10T04:24:59.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140507ea57007pt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
