\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-China c.bank reaffirms steady policy with fine-tuning\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2014\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, quotes)\par \par \uc2 BEIJING, May 6 (Reuters) - \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday it would keep monetary policy steady with timely fine-tuning to help stabilise economic growth, while introducing greater yuan flexiblity.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  will use a combination of policy tools to keep liquidity ample and maintain stable money market rates, it said in its first-quarter monetary policy implementation report.\par \par \uc2 "We will maintain appropriate liquidity and achieve reasonable growth in money supply, credit and social financing," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the report published on its website, w{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.pbc.gov"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.pbc.gov}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use policy tools, including open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reserve requirement ratios (RRR), and re-lending, re-discount, short-term liquidity \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a flexible way in response to economic changes, it said.\par \par \uc2 While maintaining its longstanding prudent monetary policy, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has started to fine-tune its stance to support the slowing economy. Last month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut RRR for rural banks and cooperative banks to shore up the weaker agricultural industry in the economy.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  also pledged to keep the yuan basically stable while pushing reforms to help introduce greater two-way flexibility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yuan hit a two-week high on Tuesday as traders suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it touched a 18-month low against the dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doubled the yuan's daily trading band against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 A survey conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the first quarter showed that 92.5 percent of Chinese trading companies believed that the scope of yuan fluctuations was "acceptable", it said.\par \par \uc2 About a third of respondents in the survey expected the yuan to depreciate in the next half-year, while 66.9 percent believed the yuan would appreciate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 PBOC\uc2  also reiterated its pledge to push interest rate reforms, including expanding the interbank market for certificates of deposit(CDs).\par \par \uc2 It also pledged to take measures to maintain financial stability and reduce systemic risks. (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Ron Popeski)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-5-9T12:32:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140506ea5600iae\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
