\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Stable But Prone to Weakness -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2014\par 02:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2360-6.2500   6.2200-6.2840 \par USD/TWD   30.110-30.180   30.000-30.240 \par USD/KRW         -               - \par USD/SGD   1.2466-1.2496   1.2400-1.2526 \par USD/MYR   3.2500-3.2650   3.2370-3.2780 \par USD/THB    32.27-32.34     32.20-32.40 \par USD/PHP    44.40-44.50     44.20-44.59 \par USD/IDR   11,500-11,570   11,470-11,670 \par USD/INR    60.11-60.41     60.00-60.71 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--supported, upside bias. Spot USD/CNY can be expected to trade with a firm tone as the technical support at 6.2360 - the base of the Bollinger uptrend channel - approaches. Overnight, the U.S. dollar index was steady, which suggests the PBOC will set the daily USD/CNY parity rate close to Monday's 6.1560. The market still expects continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan depressed versus the U.S. dollar. The yuan is down 3.1% versus the dollar this year - which ought to help export growth in the medium term. The China \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing PMI for April released yesterday cast doubt again on China's ability to sustain economic growth at current levels. The weak number could prompt speculation that the Chinese government may again introduce smaller, targeted economic stimulus packages. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2360 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2500 (psychological resistance), before 6.2840 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. USD/TWD has taken on a bearish technical stance now that it is below the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also within the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that caps at 30.180. A continuation of the recent slide in the U.S. dollar could see USD/TWD aim for the round-figure trading barrier at 30.000. Overnight, the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield rose slightly to 2.61% from around 2.58% - which could offer the greenback some support. More clarity on the U.S. Federal Reserve's view on interest rates could emerge after the Fed chief's testimony to Congress on Wednesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.110 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.180 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.240 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.300 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--possible downside bias. USD/SGD could soon take on a bearish technical bias. The U.S. dollar is dipping its toes into the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 1.2496. A Tuesday close below this level would confirm the activation of the downtrend channel that could weigh USD/SGD down to the round-figure trading barrier at 1.2400. The U.S. dollar has been under the weather due to the benchmark \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield trading at year-lows. Unless the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bond yields stage a sustained turnaround, the greenback may continue to slip broadly. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2466 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2400 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2496 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2526 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation lower. USD/MYR may drop into a lower consolidation range of 3.2370-3.2500 as the U.S. dollar remains depressed by low-yielding \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  bonds. But technical momentum for USD/MYR will remain low unless the dollar falls into the Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 3.2370. Risk appetite is slightly shaky after the disappointing China \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing PMI for April released on Monday, which could deter bullish bets on Asian risk assets. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2500 (20-day Bollinger mid and psychological support), before 3.2370 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2650 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2780 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2810 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB may linger in a technical consolidation zone of 32.27-32.40, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid line and capped by the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. U.S. dollar upside appears less likely for now due to the overhanging Cloud resistance zone that spans a fairly large range of 32.40-32.54. The multiple technical resistance levels nearby may encourage speculators to bet on USD/THB downside instead. But standing in the way of baht appreciation is the floundering Thai economy. \uc2 Thailand's finance ministry\uc2  last week warned that economic growth in the first quarter could contract due to the prolonged political impasse. Fresh elections have been set for July 20, but until then, further deterioration in economic output could lead to capital outflows that might hurt the baht. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.27 (20-day Bollinger mid line), then at 32.20 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.14 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.34 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.40 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance and top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible downside bias. A bearish technical bias for USD/PHP could be confirmed on a Tuesday close below 44.40 - which would activate the Bollinger downtrend channel on the daily chart. Upon confirmation of this bearish signal, USD/PHP may fall toward the 200-day moving average at 44.12 in the days ahead. The U.S. dollar has been trading with a heavy tone in Asia since the mixed U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday. Looking ahead, traders will be awaiting the Wednesday testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve chief Janet Yellen to Congress on the state of the U.S. economy. A bullish outlook could lift sentiment for the U.S. dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.40 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 44.20 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.12 (200-day moving average). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.50 (psychological resistance), then at 44.59 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 44.79 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation. USD/IDR is likely to trade in a consolidation range of 11,470-11,570, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid line and capped by the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. Technical signals are lacking at the moment while USD/IDR stays inside the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that spans 11,450-11,750. The main risk event for the Indonesian rupiah will likely be the July 1 presidential elections. A win for popular candidate Joko Widowo could give a slight boost to investor sentiment, though the prospect of a coalition government facing hurdles in reforming administration may keep a lid on investor exuberance. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 11,470 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 11,450 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is at 11,570 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,670 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 11,750 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible downside bias. USD/INR appears to be resilient to the downside for now, after bouncing at the entrance to the Bollinger downtrend channel on Monday. But for USD/INR to avoid the possible bearish technical signal it has to clear the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance line at 60.41. The U.S. dollar continues to trade with a slightly heavy tone after the mixed U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday. The market was likely already long the dollar before the jobs report and may be still be in the process of capitulating those positions. On the horizon, the May 16 results of India's general elections will be the focus for macro investors. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.11 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 59.81 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.41 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 60.71 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 05, 2014 20:41 ET (00:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140506ea560003e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
