\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Steady After Mixed U.S. Data -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2014\par 02:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2500-6.2600   6.2346-6.2843 \par USD/TWD   30.120-30.190   30.100-30.250 \par USD/KRW         -               - \par USD/SGD   1.2500-1.2527   1.2470-1.2556 \par USD/MYR   3.2500-3.2650   3.2360-3.2780 \par USD/THB         -               - \par USD/PHP    44.42-44.60     44.22-44.80 \par USD/IDR   11,500-11,565   11,460-11,670 \par USD/INR    60.10-60.40     59.80-60.70 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--upside bias. Spot USD/CNY is likely to remain elevated as the U.S. dollar index was stable Friday even after the U.S. jobs report. The market is primed for continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan depressed versus the U.S. dollar. The China final \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing PMI for April will be published at 0145 GMT. A weak number could again prompt speculation that the Chinese government may introduce some targeted economic stimulus packages. The U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday was mixed, showing a big jump in number of jobs added while the labor participation rate fell sharply. Hence the U.S. dollar reacted little to the data. U.S. Federal Reserve chief Janet Yellen testifies on Wednesday regarding the state of the economy. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2500 (psychological support), then at 6.2346 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2843 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--downside bias. USD/TWD has taken on a bearish technical stance now that it is below the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also within the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that caps at 30.190. A continuation of the recent slide in the U.S. dollar could see USD/TWD aim for the round-figure trading barrier at 30.000. Market sentiment is tepid on the U.S. dollar after the mixed U.S. jobs report on Friday - which triggered a drop in the U.S. bond yields, thus weighing on the greenback. More clarity on the U.S. Federal Reserve's stance could emerge after the Fed chief's testimony to Congress on Wednesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.120 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.190 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.250 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 30.300 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. An intraday range of 1.2500-1.2556 is likely for USD/SGD. The pair is caught in the consolidation zone between the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. Still lacking a catalyst after a mixed U.S. jobs report on Friday, USD/SGD may meander until a technical signal appears. The closest trigger for more USD/SGD volatility would be a Monday close below 1.2500, which could encourage U.S. dollar bears to bet on more immediate downside. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2470 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2527 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 1.2556 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2585 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR is likely to range between 3.2500-3.2650, trapped by the 20-day Bollinger mid line support and the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback has been stable since the U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday failed to invigorate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after a mixed reading which showed a large increase in jobs created, but a sharp drop in the labor participation rate. The benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield dropped significantly on Friday, which could create a downward pressure on the U.S. dollar this week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2500 (20-day Bollinger mid and psychological support), before 3.2360 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2650 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2780 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.2830 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--closed.\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP may hover within a range of 44.42-44.60 as the U.S. dollar index remained stable after Friday's mixed U.S. nonfarm payrolls report. Intraday technical signals remain weak while USD/PHP bobs inside the dead space between the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. Looking ahead, traders will be awaiting the Wednesday testimony by U.S. Federal Reserve chief Janet Yellen to Congress on the state of the U.S. economy. A bullish outlook could lift sentiment for the U.S. dollar. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.42 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 44.22 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.60 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 44.80 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), before 44.89 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR could linger in a consolidation range of 11,500-11,565, capped by the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. Technical signals are lacking at the moment while USD/IDR stays inside the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that spans 11,460-11,750. The main risk event for the Indonesian rupiah will likely be the July 1 presidential elections. A win for popular candidate Joko Widowo could give a slight boost to investor sentiment, though the prospect of a coalition government facing hurdles in reforming administration may keep a lid on investor exuberance. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,500 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 11,460 (base of Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 11,565 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,670 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--possible downside bias. A bearish technical signal for USD/INR could appear on a Monday close below 60.10. The U.S. dollar failed to rally after the mixed U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday, suggesting the market was already long the dollar and may be capitulating those positions after data showed the U.S. labor participation rate fell sharply. Entry into the Bollinger downtrend channel might send USD/INR lower to the 59.80 base of the channel and then possibly the 59.50 psychological support. On the horizon, the May 16 results of India's general elections will be the focus for macro investors. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.10 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 59.80 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.40 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 60.70 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 04, 2014 20:47 ET (00:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140505ea550000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
