\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Grinds Higher Before FOMC Decision -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,873 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2014\par 02:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2500-6.2600   6.2323-6.2835 \par USD/TWD   30.190-30.270   30.110-30.350 \par USD/KRW    1,030-1,034     1,027-1,040 \par USD/SGD   1.2540-1.2580   1.2500-1.2600 \par USD/MYR   3.2540-3.2700   3.2500-3.2800 \par USD/THB    32.19-32.28     32.10-32.35 \par USD/PHP    44.43-44.63     44.23-44.76 \par USD/IDR   11,540-11,640   11,510-11,760 \par USD/INR    60.37-60.70     60.05-61.00 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--upside bias. As the U.S. dollar index climbed overnight, the PBOC's daily USD/CNY parity rate is likely to be shifted higher. Spot USD/CNY could thus notch yet another fresh 16-month high if it surpasses Tuesday's 6.2591. The daily USD/CNY chart has been maintaining its upwards trajectory since April 9, with no sign of letting up yet. One of the reasons for the yuan's continued slippage against the dollar is suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most analysts think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's manipulation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 --an attempt to give the yuan more two-way volatility--is likely to continue. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2500 (psychological support), then at 6.2323 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2835 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation higher. USD/TWD may creep back up into the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and then consolidate. Tuesday's slightly bearish closing--below the Cloud--is likely to be nullified by overnight U.S. dollar strength which was triggered by euro weakness. USD/TWD may therefore rise and re-enter the Cloud consolidation zone that now spans 30.290-30.450. Traders are likely to keep their positions light ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve FOMC decision due later today. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.190 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.110 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.270 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 30.290 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 30.350 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--downside bias. After hitting a 5.5-year high of 1,030.1 versus the U.S. dollar early Wednesday, the South Korea won is slightly weaker as traders take profit, prompted by overnight U.S. dollar strength that is affecting other USD/Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs. However, the bearish technical bias for USD/KRW remains strong unless the dollar rises past 1,034 and thus exits the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. USD/KRW has inched higher to 1,032.0 from its last close of 1,030.6, but any spikes will likely be met by exporters' selling as they continue to repatriate earnings. South Korea's March industrial output rose 0.9% on a monthly basis, beating expectations for a 0.4% increase; but on a yearly basis the 2.7% growth was short of expectations for a 3.2% increase. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,027 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,034 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,040 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,042 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. An intraday range of 1.2540-1.2580 is likely for USD/SGD. The pair has been stuck in the no-man's land between the 20-day Bollinger mid and the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel for the last six sessions. A catalyst, possibly coming from today's U.S. FOMC decision, is necessary to break the impasse for USD/SGD. Another trigger for increased USD/SGD volatility could come from the U.S. nonfarm payrolls report due Friday. Expectations that the U.S. jobs report will be strong due to improving weather conditions ought to keep the greenback supported on dips. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2540 (20-day Bollinger mid line), then at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2457 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2580 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2618 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR may continue to bob between 3.2540-3.2700 for now, with chances for an initial blip up due to overnight U.S. dollar strength. The U.S. dollar appears to be stuck in this range for now as trading conviction is low ahead of key U.S. economic events this week, beginning with the FOMC decision later today. The U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to cut its pace of monthly bond purchases again, but investors will be focusing on hints as to the committee's timeline for lifting interest rates. Friday's U.S. nonfarm payrolls, if stronger than consensus, could nudge the Fed toward an earlier interest rate hike. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2540 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2500 (psychological support), before 3.2360 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2700 (daily bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2800 (psychological resistance), before 3.2815 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB is likely to remain stable within its current technical consolidation zone of 32.19-32.28, supported by the entrance to the Bollinger downtrend channel and capped by the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. Technical momentum on the daily charts remains weak unless the dollar either falls into the downtrend channel at 32.19 or rallies into the uptrend channel at 32.38. The multiple technical resistance levels close by, including the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone at 32.35, may encourage speculators to bet on USD/THB downside instead. But standing in the way of baht appreciation is the floundering Thai economy. \uc2 Thailand's finance ministry\uc2  on Tuesday warned that economic growth in the first quarter could contract due to the prolonged political conflict weighing on business confidence and private spending, not to mention tourism. A deterioration in economic output could lead to capital outflows that might hurt the baht, said bank analysts. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.19 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.10 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.28 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 32.35 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 32.38 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation higher. USD/PHP may rebound slightly within its current consolidation range of 44.43-44.63 due to a bounce in the U.S. dollar index overnight. Intraday technical signals remain weak while USD/PHP bobs inside the dead space between the daily Bollinger downtrend channel and the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. On Monday, the Malaysian state investment firm Khazanah said it will buy a 8% stake in Philippine property developer 8990 Holdings for approximately $66 million. The investment is a vote of confidence for the Philippines' growth potential. A possible roadblock to peso strength could be the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision at its FOMC meeting later today. If the Fed appears more upbeat on the economy, the market will be primed for more hawkishness in the near future and thus be more bullish on the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.43 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 44.23 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.63 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 44.76 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 44.80 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR may reverse Tuesday's slight drop and head back toward the top of the Bollinger uptrend channel as traders eye the overnight rise of the U.S. dollar index as a catalyst for a USD/IDR rally. The U.S. dollar remains well-supported by the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 11,540 and also by the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone currently at 11,510. As long as these technical supports hold, the U.S. dollar is more likely to rise than fall. Traders are focusing on the U.S. FOMC decision today, looking for hints of increased hawkishness from the committee that could translate into an earlier-than-expected interest rate rise. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,540 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,510 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 11,500 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 11,640 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,760 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 29 Apr 2014 20:51 ET  USD/Asia Grinds Higher Before FOMC Decision -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. USD/INR may bounce higher within its technical consolidation zone that now spans 60.37-60.70. The U.S. dollar rebounded overnight due to euro weakness, lifting most USD/Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs higher Wednesday. If the greenback rallies ahead of the U.S. FOMC decision later today, USD/INR could regain its bullish technical bias--contingent on a daily close above 60.70 and thereby within the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Re-entry into the uptrend channel will increase the likelihood of near-term rupee weakness. External factors, such as U.S. economic data, will continue to dictate the rupee's direction until the May 16 results of India's general elections. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.37 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 60.05 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.70 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 61.02 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 29, 2014 20:51 ET (00:51 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140430ea4u0003p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\pi