 is at 6.2500 (psychological support), then at 6.2298 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2823 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation. USD/TWD continues to tread water inside the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone. The interim trading range demarcated by the Cloud that spans 30.290-30.450 will likely trap USD/TWD as traders keep positions light ahead of the U.S. nonfarm payrolls and FOMC meeting this week. The greenback is likely to remain supported on dips as the benchmark U.S. 10-year government bond yield remains above 2.70%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.290 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 30.200 (psychological support), before 30.180 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.380 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.450 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 30.500 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--downside bias. USD/KRW dropped back into the Bollinger downtrend channel as of its Monday close, lending a bearish bias to the U.S. dollar this week. USD/KRW opened lower Tuesday following overnight greenback weakness, and may now head for the downtrend channel's base at 1,028. Strong capital inflows have been helping the South Korea won to strengthen despite broadly bullish views on the U.S. unit ahead of the U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday, said a trader. The U.S. dollar has been firm against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back of the elevated U.S. 10-year Treasury yield - which reveals that investors expect the U.S. Federal Reserve may turn more hawkish on improving jobs data. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,028 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,035 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,040 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,044 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation. USD/SGD is caught in a narrow intraday range of 1.2544-1.2588, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid line and capped by the entrance to the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Traders are likely to stay on the sidelines ahead of the U.S. FOMC meeting which concludes Wednesday and the U.S. nonfarm payrolls report due Friday. Expectations that the U.S. jobs report will be strong due to improving weather conditions ought to keep the greenback supported on dips. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2544 (20-day Bollinger mid line), then at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2457 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2588 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2631 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. USD/MYR appears unable to break higher and enter the Bollinger uptrend channel after twice, in the last two sessions, failing to close above 3.2710. This indicates the dollar's rally has run out of steam and may hence consolidate lower for now. Waiting at 3.2540 is the 20-day Bollinger mid support which will likely prop up the dollar on dips. As long as the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield stays above 2.70% - implying that investors expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to announce another cut in bond purchases after the FOMC meeting on Wednesday - the dollar is likely to remain buoyant. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2540 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2500 (psychological support), before 3.2360 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2710 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2800 (psychological resistance), before 3.2815 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation. USD/THB may range trade within a technical consolidation zone of 32.19-32.28, capped by the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. Technical momentum on the daily charts remains weak unless the dollar either falls into the Bollinger downtrend channel at 32.19 or rallies into the uptrend channel at 32.38. The multiple technical ceilings close by, including the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone, may make it more likely that speculators will bet on USD/THB downside. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.19 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.10 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.28 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), then at 32.34 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 32.38 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--possible downside bias. USD/PHP's drop on Monday, possibly triggered by news of strong foreign investment in the Philippines to come, may extend lower and activate the daily Bollinger downtrend channel. On a Tuesday close below 44.44, USD/PHP will take on a bearish technical bias that could send the dollar down to 44.22 and then the round-figure trading barrier of 44.00. On Monday, the Malaysian state investment firm Khazanah said it will buy a 8% stake in Philippine property developer 8990 Holdings for approximately $66 million. The investment is a vote of confidence for the Philippines' growth potential. A possible roadblock to more peso strength could be the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision at its FOMC meeting which concludes Wednesday. If the Fed keeps trimming its pace of monthly Treasury purchases as expected, the market will be primed for more hawkishness in the near future and thus be more bullish on the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.44 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 44.22 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.67 (20-day Bollinger mid and Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 44.80 (psychological resistance), before 44.88 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--upside bias. USD/IDR is well-supported at 11,520 where the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone coincides with the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. As long as this technical floor holds, the U.S. dollar is more likely to rise than fall. The main driver for greenback strength ahead will be the U.S. Federal Reserve's FOMC meeting that concludes Wednesday, and the U.S nonfarm payrolls report due Friday. Affirmation of the improving U.S. hiring environment - which will lead to an earlier lifting of the base U.S. lending rate - will fuel the dollar higher. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,520 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 11,415 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is at 11,630 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 11,760 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. USD/INR may hover within a technical consolidation zone between 60.35-60.68. The dollar's drop out of the Bollinger uptrend channel on Monday indicates the rally may have been exhausted. A fresh catalyst, which could appear after the U.S. Federal Reserve's FOMC meeting on Wednesday, is needed to push USD/INR back into the uptrend channel. External factors, mainly from U.S. data, will continue to dictate the rupee's direction until the May 16 results of India's general elections. In the background, improving views for India's economy may provide additional support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The IMF said in its latest regional survey that it expects India to grow 5.4% in 2014, up from its 4.4% last year. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.35 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 59.68 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.68 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier), before 61.02 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 28, 2014 21:05 ET (01:05 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140429ea4t0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
