\par\par \b \uc2 China  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Regulator: 1Q Current Account Surplus $7.2 Bln -- Update -2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Richard Silk   \par \uc2 548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 2014\par 10:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BEIJING--China's broadest measure of trade with the world posted its smallest quarterly surplus in three years, suggesting that upward pressure on the yuan may ease in the long run.\par \par \uc2 China's first-quarter current-account surplus, the difference between exports and imports in goods and services as well as one-time transfers of funds, shrank to $7.2 billion, the \uc2 State Administration of \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday, representing 0.3% of gross domestic product. That is down from a $44 billion surplus in the final quarter of 2013, and reflects an unusually poor export performance in the first three months of the year.\par \par \uc2 The $7.2 billion balance "seems like a lot of money in dollar terms, but as a share of GDP it's small," said Zhiwei Zhang, a Hong Kong-based economist at Nomura.\par \par \uc2 China keeps a tight grip on the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some lawmakers and businesses in the U.S. and elsewhere say China's big current-account surpluses in the past showed the yuan is undervalued, giving its exporters an unfair advantage in markets with other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the shrinking balance blunts those arguments. China's current account surplus peaked at 10.1% of GDP in 2007, according to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 . Last year, it was 2.1% of GDP. Some economists now argue that the yuan could be close to fair value.\par \par \uc2 "If we look at medium-term Chinese competitiveness, the renminbi could already be slightly overvalued," said Li-Gang Liu, an economist at \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yuan has appreciated by almost 10% against the U.S. dollar since 2010, when China relaxed its exchange-rate regime. But it has lost about 3% so far this year, an unexpected drop that most observers pinned on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is eager to introduce more two-way volatility into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discourage speculators, analysts say.\par \par \uc2 China also posted a first-quarter surplus of $118.3 billion on the capital and financial account, which measures flows of investment funds in and out of the country, down from $127 billion in the last quarter of 2013. Both current account and capital account data are preliminary and subject to revision.\par \par \uc2 Capital inflows are driven mainly by the difference in interest rates inside and outside the country, Mr. Liu said. The world is still awash with cheap money from the U.S. and Japanese quantitative easing programs, with benchmark interest rates in both countries close to zero. Interbank rates in China stand at about 3.5%. Investors who are able to borrow offshore and invest in China stand to make a profit from exploiting the difference.\par \par \uc2 Capital inflows also contribute to upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, they could soon go into reverse as interest rates begin to rise in the developed world, said Li Cui, an economist at \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  in Hong Kong, who also believes the yuan is close to fair value.\par \par \uc2 Mark Magnier and Liyan Qi contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Richard Silk at richard.silk@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 25-04-14 0856GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140425ea4p0006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
