\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/CNY Has Upside Bias\b0\par\par\uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2014\par 03:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0900 [Dow Jones] USD/CNY--upside bias. Though the U.S. dollar index slipped a tad overnight, implying a likely lower PBOC daily USD/CNY benchmark rate, spot USD/CNY could still be on the rise. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, buying the U.S. dollar in the spot market and selling the yuan to depress its value. The continuation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - despite verbal warnings from the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform on track - will likely encourage traders to bet on further yuan weakness to come. The yuan hit a new 16-month low of 6.2466 on Wednesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2300 (psychological support), then at 6.2213 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2767 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 24-04-14 0114GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140424ea4o00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
