\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Likely Capped By Technical Barriers -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 2014\par 02:59\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2300-6.2500   6.2213-6.2767 \par USD/TWD   30.200-30.320   30.180-30.340 \par USD/KRW    1,037-1,040     1,030-1,048 \par USD/SGD   1.2545-1.2589   1.2500-1.2600 \par USD/MYR   3.2530-3.2700   3.2500-3.2800 \par USD/THB    32.31-32.41     32.21-32.50 \par USD/PHP    44.66-44.72     44.50-44.80 \par USD/IDR   11,600-11,630   11,555-11,760 \par USD/INR    61.00-61.30     60.93-61.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--upside bias. Though the U.S. dollar index slipped a tad overnight, implying a likely lower PBOC daily USD/CNY benchmark rate, spot USD/CNY could still be on the rise. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, buying the U.S. dollar in the spot market and selling the yuan to depress its value. The continuation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - despite verbal warnings from the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  that \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  should keep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reform on track - will likely encourage traders to bet on further yuan weakness to come. The yuan hit a new 16-month low of 6.2466 on Wednesday. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2300 (psychological support), then at 6.2213 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2200 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2500 (round-figure trading barrier), before 6.2767 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--possible upside bias. USD/TWD may be about to take a bullish technical stance as it makes its way past the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that has been capping around 30.320. On a Thursday close above this mark, USD/TWD will likely advance toward the Bollinger uptrend channel that starts at 30.460. A confirmed entry into the uptrend channel would accelerate the dollar's rally. The greenback is likely to maintain its recent dominance as the benchmark U.S. 10-year government bond yield remains above 2.70%. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.200 (psychological support), then at 30.180 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 30.160 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.320 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 30.460 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.500 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation. USD/KRW has been very well-capped around 1,040 despite the broader rise of the U.S. dollar in Asia this week. Strong dollar-selling, likely by South Korean exporters repatriating earnings, is likely to be the reason for the won's resilience. USD/KRW lost its bearish bias after it broke out of the Bollinger downtrend channel, and may now consolidate between 1,037-1,048, capped by the 20-day Bollinger mid at 1,050. The U.S. dollar has been firm this week on the back of the elevated U.S. 10-year Treasury yield - which suggests that investors expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to stay slightly hawkish at the FOMC meeting next meeting. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,037 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1,030 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1,025 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,040 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,048 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1,050 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation higher. USD/SGD has a mild bullish potential now that it has crossed the 20-day Bollinger mid line. A Thursday close above 1.2589 would place USD/SGD inside the daily Bollinger uptrend channel - which would encourage more traders to bet on U.S. dollar strength in the near future. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2  maintaining its stance for gradual appreciation for the Singapore dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been weakening versus the U.S. dollar due to external factors. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield, which has been on the rise lately, has been propelling the greenback upwards this week. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2545 (20-day Bollinger mid line), then at 1.2500 (round-figure trading barrier and daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2457 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1.2589 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), before 1.2633 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation. The doji candlestick on Wednesday suggests the USD/MYR rally has run out of steam and the dollar may consolidate for now. A likely intraday range would be 3.2530-3.2700, supported by the 20-day Bollinger mid line and capped by the entrance to the Bollinger uptrend channel. As long as the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield stays above 2.70% - implying that investors expect the U.S. Federal Reserve to keep cutting bond purchases - the dollar is likely to remain buoyant. The U.S. Federal Reserve FOMC meeting spanning 29-30 April may provide new guidance regarding monetary policy. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2530 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 3.2500 (psychological support), before 3.2360 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2700 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 3.2800 (psychological resistance), before 3.2815 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation, possible upside bias. USD/THB is likely to tread water within a narrow range of 32.31-32.41, supported by the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud which coincides with the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance thus creating a strong technical floor. The \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  on Wednesday kept its key interest rate unchanged as most had expected. The on-hold rate decision was expected since the BOT has already slashed the base interest rate twice since November, bringing it to its lowest level in more than three years. The cut in rates has been described by some analysts as a blunt tool for stimulating an economy burdened by political impasse. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.31 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 32.21 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.11 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.41 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.50 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--consolidation. USD/PHP's rally on Wednesday bumped into technical resistance at 44.69-44.72 that managed to stop the dollar's advance. This could trigger profit-taking by short-term speculators who were already long on the U.S. dollar. USD/PHP could therefore consolidate for now until a catalyst for further U.S. dollar strength appears. The guiding force for the dollar this week has been the elevated U.S. 10-year Treasury yield - an indication of investors' expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve's next move at its 29-30 April FOMC meeting. If the Fed keeps trimming its pace of monthly Treasury purchases as expected, the market will be primed for more hawkishness in the near future, and thus be more bullish on the greenback. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.66 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 44.50 (psychological support), before 44.48 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.72 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 44.80 (psychological resistance), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation. USD/IDR's rally stalled at the daily Ichimoku Cloud technical resistance zone looming around 11,630 - indicating reduced likelihood for the dollar to rise again today. The resilience of the technical ceiling could trigger a profit-taking selloff that might weigh USD/IDR down slightly toward 11,550 where the Bollinger band (standard deviation 2) awaits. The rupiah has fallen almost 2% this week and may extend its slide next week as the market focuses on the U.S. FOMC meeting 29-30 April that might trigger more dollar-bullishness. If the Fed again hints at interest rate hikes to come once the bond-buying program has been fully withdrawn, the greenback will likely rally. There seems to be little respite ahead for the rupiah; its weakness was triggered by a poor polling result for the popular PDI-P party in the legislative elections. The party will now have to form a coalition for the presidential election on 1 July, giving it less clout in government even if it manages an eventual victory. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,600 (psychological support), then at 11,555 (upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2), before 11,500 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 11,630 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 11,760 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), before 11,800 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--limited upside. USD/INR could be running out of headroom on the daily chart. The Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone that overhangs at 61.30 will likely cap the dollar's rise for now. Unless a fresh catalyst appears for the greenback, USD/INR may retreat after having tested this technical ceiling. A pullback in USD/INR could give the rupee some respite, but the rupee may still remain vulnerable in the days ahead as the market has an underlying bullish view for the U.S. dollar ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's FOMC meeting next week. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 60.93 (upper Bollinger band standard deviation 2), before 60.60 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 61.30 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 61.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 23 Apr 2014 20:59 ET  USD/Asia Likely Capped By Technical Barriers -- -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 23, 2014 20:59 ET (00:59 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140424ea4o0003s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
