\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips after weaker midpoint, may head for fresh low\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2014\par 06:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Spot yuan slips 0.11 pct to 6.2340/dlr at midday\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets midpoint slightly lower for 3 straight days\par     * But no sign of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading\par     * Yuan seen falling below 6.2370, its March 21 low\par \par     By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par     SHANGHAI, April 22 (Reuters) - China's yuan eased against\par the dollar on Tuesday after a weaker official midpoint fixing\par for the third straight day, signalling that the monetary\par authorities have no intention of letting the yuan reverse its\par recent weakness for now, traders said.\par     However, there was no sign that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to depress the yuan either.\par     Assessing the recent midpoint fixings and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's\par actions, traders forecast the yuan was likely to soon fall below\par 6.2370 versus the dollar, its recent low hit on March 21, but it\par may find a floor around 6.25 per dollar in coming weeks.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  appear to toe a cautious line, maintaining the\par yuan's recent weakness but also not to push it sharply lower to\par spark panic," said a dealer at a Chinese commercial bank in\par Shanghai.\par     "But sentiment towards the yuan has been greatly weakened by\par its sharp depreciation this year, with companies retaining more\par dollars on hand recently. This underlines the possibility for\par the yuan to hit a fresh low again and soon."\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.2340 per dollar at midday,\par 0.11 percent weaker than Monday's close, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixed\par its midpoint at 6.1610, down 0.03 percent from Monday.\par     The yuan has depreciated 2.89 percent so far this year under\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's guidance, hitting a low of 6.2370 on March 21, its \par weakest in more than a year.\par     The depreciation is due in part to apparent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  earlier this year in the form of dollar purchases\par by state banks, but traders say such purchases have diminished\par in recent weeks.\par     The shift to holding the yuan steadier without letting it\par reverse its weakness suggests continued efforts to deter\par speculative bets on the yuan's rise.\par     Thus, traders said the yuan was likely to move mainly\par between 6.20 and 6.25 against the dollar in the coming weeks.\par     The market believes speculators built up heavy, long\par positions on the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  based on the view that it\par would not weaken below 6.20. If the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  keeps the yuan below\par 6.20 for a long period it will strike a heavy blow on punters,\par traders say. \par  \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                       Current    Previous  Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1610     6.1591      -0.03\par  Spot yuan                  6.2340     6.2274      -0.11\par  Divergence from midpoint*  1.18                 \par  (pct)                                           \par  Spot change ytd                                 -2.89\par  Spot change since 2005                          32.76\par  revaluation                                     \par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par     \par The offshore yuan market at a glance:\par  Instrument                     Current  Difference\par                                          from onshore\par                                          (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan             6.2349   -0.01\par  Offshore non-deliverable       6.2650   -1.66\par  forwards                                \par  *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - US warns China over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  depreciation \par     - Capital flows, improving trade to prop up yuan in\par H2   \par     - Dim sum bonds mark record quarter in Hong Kong\par  \par     - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par     - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan spot performance versus midpoint after trading band\par widened \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/jyz38v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's yuan, other emerging mkt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  vs dollar \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/xyd46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performance INTERACTIVE GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.co