ubside late March and efforts to keep it from rebounding are challenged by a falling dollar.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.1490 compared with Tuesday's 6.1527.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts fell to 6.2210/6.2260 from 6.2305/6.2335 late Tuesday--implying a 0.5% fall by the yuan over the next year.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at 6.1991 yuan compared with 6.1986 yuan late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Wynne Wang at wynne.wang@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 09-04-14 0949GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140409ea490007w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
