\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Sinks as Longs Capitulate -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2014\par 03:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.1907-6.2000   6.1800-6.2370 \par USD/TWD    30.220-30.310   30.000-30.400 \par USD/KRW     1,040-1,050     1,035-1,055 \par USD/SGD    1.2500-1.2550   1.2482-1.2568 \par USD/MYR    3.2300-3.2400   3.2150-3.2500 \par USD/THB     32.24-32.36     32.11-32.50 \par USD/PHP     44.69-44.80     44.50-44.82 \par USD/IDR    11,245-11,320   11,000-11,500 \par USD/INR     59.50-60.00     59.00-60.50 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--possible downside bias. Spot USD/CNY may drop below the round-figure trading barrier at 6.2000 and then fall out of the Bollinger uptrend channel losing its bullish bias. A downturn for the U.S. dollar index overnight is likely to lead to a much lower daily USD/CNY benchmark rate--possibly below the 6.1500 level--which would weigh on spot USD/CNY. On a confirmed break of the uptrend channel USD/CNY may retreat even further in the near term toward the 20-day Bollinger mid at 6.1290. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may retreat from aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yuan weak after a \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  official said it is monitoring recent alleged devaluation of the yuan post-band widening. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.1907 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1500 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 6.2000 (round figure trading barrier), then at 6.2370 (12-month high), then at 6.2520 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation lower. USD/TWD has broken the daily Ichimoku Cloud support and is now inside the Bollinger downtrend channel making its way to the bottom of the cloud at 30.050 which is the next technical floor. If this barrier is breached by the end of the day it increases the likelihood the dollar will fall further in the near term. The U.S. dollar sank overnight against the majors triggering selling across USD/Asia as well. The U.S. 10-year Treasury yield continues to inch down indicating lowered expectations for the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise interest rates in the near future thus motivating USD-bears to sell the U.S. unit. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.220 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 30.050 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone), before 30.000 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.310 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and top of Ichimoku Cloud), then at 30.400 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance), before 30.500 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--consolidation with downside bias. USD/KRW gaps much lower to open at 1,046.0 versus its last close of 1,052.2 reflecting an overnight fall in the U.S. dollar index. USD/KRW now appears oversold, extended past the lower Bollinger band (standard deviation 2), suggesting immediate downside potential has been exhausted. The dollar may hence consolidate for now before making another move lower. The sharp drop in the U.S. dollar has been blamed on capitulation as the market takes profit on long-dollar positions that were put on before last week's U.S. nonfarm payrolls. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,040 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,035 (base of monthly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,050 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1,055 (top of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,058 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--consolidation with downside bias. Following selling in the U.S. dollar across the majors as well as the emerging markets USD/SGD has sunk to the bottom of the Bollinger downtrend channel and is now staging a small relief rally--which is likely to be capped around 1.2550. The overnight weakness in the U.S. dollar was likely a result of profit-taking on long-USD positions, a trader said. Ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2 's policy statement on Monday a contrarian view is that the MAS may shift its stance from gradual appreciation for the Singapore dollar toward a more neutral one--which may trigger Singapore dollar weakness. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2500 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2482 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2450 (psychological resistance). Immediate resistance is at 1.2550 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2568 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--consolidation with downside bias. Following selling late Tuesday USD/MYR is rebounding after briefly extending past the lower Bollinger band (standard deviation 2)--a statistical average that suggests a likely amplitude of fluctuation based on recent price movements. The overextension past the lower Bollinger band indicates the move has gone too far too fast. USD/MYR may therefore consolidate for now while dollar bears wait for a more optimal level to sell again. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2300 (psychological support), before 3.2150 (base of weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2400 (psychological resistance), then at 3.2500 (psychological resistance), before 3.2580 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--possible downside bias. USD/THB may enter the Bollinger downtrend channel on a daily close below 32.24. Selling in the U.S. dollar across the board sank USD/THB to as low as 32.22 from around 32.44 on Tuesday triggering a capitulation of long-USD positions. The retreat of the U.S. dollar may continue on confirmation of the bearish technical signal that is the Bollinger downtrend channel. Investors have so far been closing their eyes to the political drama unfolding in Thailand. There may be more clashes as the 'Red Shirts' mobilize to defend the Yingluck Shinawatra government against its opponents. Markets will wait for the announcement of fresh elections after the Constitutional Court ruled an election Feb. 2 was invalid. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.24 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 32.11 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.00 (round-figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 32.36 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 32.50 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), before 32.53 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP has a mild bearish bias now that it has broken through the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone that had provided support at 44.80-44.82. The U.S. dollar may turn more bearish on a Wednesday close below 44.69 which would place it inside the USD/PHP Bollinger downtrend channel. The downtrend channel would guide USD/PHP to the next technical support at 44.50. A trimming of long-USD positions in response to the slightly weak U.S. nonfarm payrolls report on Friday against a backdrop of a gradually declining U.S. 10-year Treasury yield has been weighing on the U.S. unit. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.69 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 44.50 (psychological support and base of Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.80 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), then at 44.82 (top of Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 44.87 (20-day Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. The Indonesian rupiah is likely to rally as legislative voting begins Wednesday. Broad dollar weakness, however, may be the main reason USD/IDR may drop to 11,000 in the near term. But if the PDI-P party manages a strong showing, which would set the stage for a victory for presidential candidate Joko Widodo, the rupiah may get another boost. On Tuesday the Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept base interest rates on hold as expected because of receding inflation readings. The USD/IDR Bollinger downtrend channel--which indicates the rupiah is likely to appreciate versus the U.S. unit--will stay in play as long as the dollar remains below 11,320 by the end of the day. The downtrend channel may lead the rupiah to the round-figure trading barrier at 11,000 which is also the bottom of the channel and hence a technical support as well. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,000 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,320 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,650 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--downside bias. USD/INR is likely to drop sharply to reflect U.S. dollar weakness over the past two days as the market reopens after the Tuesday break. The rupee may rally to 59.50 versus the U.S. dollar in reaction to selling in the U.S. unit that has boosted regional Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. General elections in India, which began Monday and will last five weeks, may be another trigger for more rupee strength. Any indication of a positive result for the anticorruption, pro-business BJP party will push USD/INR toward the weekly technical support at 58.36. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 59.50 (psychological support), before 59.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 60.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 8 Apr 2014 21:10 ET  USD/Asia Sinks as Longs Capitulate -- Asia Daily -2-\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 08, 2014 21:10 ET (01:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140409ea490006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
