\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Likely Lower as Risk Appetite Rises -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2014\par 02:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY   6.2000-6.2370   6.1800-6.2500 \par USD/TWD   30.400-30.500   30.300-30.600 \par USD/KRW    1,056-1,060    1,050-1,065 \par USD/SGD   1.2562-1.2600   1.2555-1.2607 \par USD/MYR   3.2500-3.2640   3.2430-3.2715 \par USD/THB    32.23-32.35     32.11-32.47 \par USD/PHP    44.70-44.85     44.59-44.88 \par USD/IDR   11,300-11,390   11,050-11,500 \par USD/INR    60.00-60.50     59.50-60.57 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. Technical signs of USD/CNY topping out on the daily chart suggest that the dollar may consolidate slightly lower. The doji candlestick on Monday followed by the bearish close on Tuesday indicates that upside momentum may be fading. The slight overnight weakness of the U.S. dollar index could also weigh the PBOC benchmark USD/CNY rate down--which would drag on spot USD/CNY. While financial markets around the world are in risk-taking mode, the yuan has struggled to appreciate as niggling concerns remain that China's economy is not doing as well as it should be. Speculation that the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is going to keep the yuan weak via direct market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is another reason hampering a yuan rebound. \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index released Tuesday showed a slight improvement to 50.3 from February's 50.2--which was also the median forecast. The China HSBC Manufacturing PMI however, revealed a pessimistic outlook from manufacturers--the competing PMI survey fell to 48.0 from 48.5 the previous month. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.2000 (round figure trading barrier), then at 6.1800 (psychological support), before 6.1771 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.2370 (12-month high), then at 6.2373 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 6.2500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--consolidation lower. USD/TWD may slip again and re-test the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 30.400 as risk appetite is likely to get a boost from a continuation of the stock market rally in the U.S. overnight. The safe haven greenback has been losing appeal as investors flock back into emerging market assets after reassurances from the U.S. Federal Reserve that interest rates will stay low to promote job growth. Suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a regular basis has been keeping the Taiwan dollar from gaining excessively. The official Taiwan manufacturing PMI data released Tuesday showed a jump higher to 60.6 versus 50.3 in February, though the competing \uc2 HSBC\uc2  survey showed a drop to 52.7 from 54.7 the previous month. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.400 (20-day Bollinger mid support), before 30.300 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone and entrance to Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.500 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.600 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 30.667 (2.5-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--downside bias. USD/KRW gaps lower Wednesday, opening at 1,056.5 from its previous close of 1,058.5 to reflect overnight dollar weakness. The safe haven U.S. dollar has been under pressure recently as risk appetite makes a comeback. USD/KRW has now reached the entrance to the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel at 1,056--a technical support--and may stabilize for now. On a Friday close below 1,056, more USD/KRW downside can be expected over the medium term. The South Korea \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing Purchasing Managers Index released Tuesday showed a rise to 50.4 for March versus 49.8 the previous month, indicating improvement in the economy. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,056 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,050 (round figure trading barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1,060 (psychological resistance), then at 1,065 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1,069 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--downside bias. USD/SGD is likely to be well-capped by the Bollinger downtrend channel ceiling at 1.2607 and could keep heading lower as the U.S. dollar faces broad weakness in Asia. The rebound in risk appetite, sparked by U.S. Federal Reserve chairwoman Janet Yellen emphasizing job creation, has been depressing the greenback and lifting Asian assets this week. However, dealers have noted buying on dips in USD/SGD due to bullish bets being placed ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore\uc2 's policy meeting sometime next week. Some traders think there is a chance that the MAS could shift its stance from gradual appreciation for the Singapore dollar toward a more neutral one--which would have the kneejerk effect of triggering Singapore dollar weakness. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2562 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 1.2555 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2500 (round-figure barrier). Immediate resistance is at 1.2600 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 1.2607 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 1.2659 (20-dau Bollinger mid resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--downside bias. USD/MYR is on a bearish path within the daily Bollinger downtrend channel toward weekly support at 3.2430. The greenback is under pressure from two bearish technical indicators--it is below the Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone and also inside the Bollinger downtrend channel which caps at 3.2640. If USD/MYR closes Friday below 3.2430, it will also be inside the weekly Bollinger downtrend channel and could continue sliding to 3.2000 in the weeks ahead. Until the release of U.S. non-farm payrolls on Friday, the dollar will likely remain soft. The U.S. nonfarm payrolls report, if it surprises either side of expectations, will be the next trigger that could dictate the dollar's direction. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.2500 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel and psychological support), before 3.2430 (weekly Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 3.2640 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 3.2715 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.2790 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--consolidation lower. USD/THB has dropped below the 20-day Bollinger mid support at 32.35, increasing the chances of further USD/THB weakness. The U.S. dollar could next slip to the entrance to the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 32.23. Even as ongoing politics-related violence threaten to derail investor confidence in Thailand, the overall recovery in global risk appetite this week has boosted emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  broadly. The ruling by the Thai Constitutional Court that the election held on February 2 was invalid will lead to new elections and possibly more protests ahead. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.23 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 32.11 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 32.35 (20-day Bollinger mid), then at 32.47 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 32.51 (daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--downside bias. USD/PHP is likely to break downside support at 44.70 where the bottom of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone lies. A Wednesday close below this mark would suggest the dollar extends its fall to 44.59--which if breached as well would lead to the next technical support at 44.30. Risk appetite has been returning with gusto following reassurance from the U.S. Federal Reserve that job creation is still the priority. The market appears to have looked past the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raising banks' reserve requirement ratio last Thursday--an effort to tame excessive credit growth. The restraint in the lending ratio was viewed as a small first step toward raising interest rates. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 44.70 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud support), then at 44.59 (entrance to daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 44.30 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 44.85 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 44.88 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 45.00 (round-figure trading barrier).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--downside bias. USD/IDR is likely to break the 4-month low of 11,245 and head for the 11,200 psychological support as the dollar slips further on improvement in risk appetite. The daily Bollinger downtrend channel has been a bearish technical influence on the dollar, now capping USD/IDR at 11,390. The downtrend channel suggests the near-term target for the rupiah is 11,050 where the bottom of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel meets the weekly Bollinger mid line. Risk appetite received a big boost on Tuesday when Indonesia published its trade balance data. A bigger-than-expected trade surplus of $790 million in February from a $430.6 million deficit in January drove the local stock market index up 2.2%. Risk appetite for Indonesian assets is expected to remain strong leading up to the presidential elections in June. The Indonesia \uc2 HSBC\uc2  manufacturing PMI survey released shortly before the trade balance data showed a slight decline to 50.1 in March versus 50.5 in February. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 11,300 (psychological support), then at 11,245 (4-month low), before 11,050 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 11,390 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 11,500 (psychological resistance), before 11,730 (20-day Bollinger mid).\par \par \uc2 1 Apr 2014 20:54 ET  USD/Asia Likely Lower as Risk Appetite Rises -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation with downside bias. USD/INR appears to be stabilizing near the 60.00 round-figure trading barrier but the Bollinger downtrend channel that currently caps at 60.86 will keep the dollar looking bearish in the near term. After the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  kept interest rates unchanged Tuesday as the market expected, the rupee barely reacted. The rupee may have been overbought in recent days, the technical charts suggest. USD/INR was overstretched past the lower Bollinger band (standard deviation 2) since late last week, suggesting that a pullback could occur before fresh sellers would be tempted to enter. Fundamentally, the rupee is still looking attractive ahead of general elections commencing next week. A potential change of leadership could herald more business-friendly policies and a tougher approach to corruption. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 60.00 (round-figure trading barrier), then at 59.50 (psychological support), before 59.00 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 60.50 (psychological resistance), then at 60.57 (weekly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), before 60.86 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 April 01, 2014 20:54 ET (00:54 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140402ea420003l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
