\par\par \b \uc2 China's Yuan Bounces Back-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 By Fiona Law   \par \uc2 459 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 09:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--China's yuan is set for its biggest weekly gain in 21/2 years, rebounding from an unprecedented tumble since mid-February that has been steered by authorities in Beijing seeking to kick out speculators.\par \par \uc2 The roller-coaster ride for the normally steady \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes as China says its wants bigger swings and to allow more market-oriented movements as the country moves forward with financial reforms. Premier \uc2 Li Keqiang\uc2  said Wednesday at the nation's annual legislative session that the 1% daily trading band would be expanded.\par \par \uc2 The yuan usually trades less than 0.2% either way each day because of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It climbed 0.8% this week, erasing much of the 1.3% fall in the past two weeks that had spooked investors. On Friday, it strengthened to as much as 6.10 yuan to the dollar, and changed hands recently at 6.11 at noon in Shanghai.\par \par \uc2 Last time the yuan, also known as the renminbi, recorded a similar weekly surge in value was in mid-August 2011.\par \par \uc2 "The [sharp rise] is entirely expected because the authorities have no intention of persistently weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it's natural for renminbi to have a significant rebound after a big drop," said Robert Minikin, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 The moves toward increased volatility, and eventually less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , come as \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also pursues an ambitious plan to internationalize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and increase its use outside the world's second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 The yuan's recent tumble caught many money managers by surprise. Many had been betting on further gains, following a rise of about 30% since July 2005 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was revalued and ended a decadelong peg to the dollar. Many companies, too, had placed leveraged bets using structured products that profit from gains in the yuan and cause losses if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  drops.\par \par \uc2 "This is a new norm for China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Bigger swing in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be seen in coming days and weeks," Mr. Minikin said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the dramatic ups and downs, offshore yuan debt--nicknamed dim-sum bonds--haven't lost steam, enjoying robust support from fund managers who still believe in the long-term prospect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and like the lucrative interest rates offered by these debt.\par \par \uc2 The latest evidence of this came late Thursday with the Hong Kong unit of \uc2 China Construction Bank Corp\uc2 . selling 4 billion yuan ($654 million) of dim-sum bonds, the largest offering in one batch by a nongovernment borrower, according to people familiar with the deal.\par \par \uc2 Write to Fiona Law at fiona.law@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 07-03-14 0816GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020140307ea370006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
