\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan rises for 3rd straight day, \uc2 PBOC\uc2  moves to sidelines\b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 06:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Company dollar sales dominate as \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  stays sidelined\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have already achieved goal of shaking out\par speculators\par     * Data shows intensified \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   in Jan\par     * Academic questions \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy\par \par     By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par     SHANGHAI, March 6 (Reuters) - China's yuan strengthened for\par a third straight session on Thursday as corporate dollar sales\par dominated amid signs that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was staying on the\par sidelines, allowing the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to recover from its\par recent weakness.\par     Dollar purchases by state banks -- a sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 designed to weaken the yuan --\par appeared to subside this week, freeing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reverse a\par large chunk of its losses since mid-January, traders said.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may feel that it has reached its goal to warn\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculators by engineering the latest round of yuan\par depreciation," said a dealer at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "The market believes the yuan may stabilise in the near\par term, possibly staging some decent rebounds and returning to a\par lingering long-term trend for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate."\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.1159 per dollar at midday,\par or 0.20 percent stronger than Wednesday's close after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par fixed its official midpoint marginally higher at 6.1249 from\par Wednesday's 6.1257, possibly another sign that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par would be willing to let the yuan stabilise for now.\par     In the longer term, the world's second-largest economy still\par faces heavy capital inflows under both the current account and\par capital accounts -- which means the yuan still has potential to\par appreciate gradually, traders said.\par     In a related development, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Chinese commercial\par banks purchased 437.4 billion yuan ($85 billion) worth of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on a net basis in January, according to a\par Reuters calculation based on \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  data released on Wednesday.\par     That was up sharply from 272.9 billion they bought in\par December, indicating stepped up official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  into the\par yuan/dollar trading, traders said.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and state banks have consistently bought foreign\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flowing into the country over the past decade or so\par to help the government to control the pace of yuan appreciation\par against the dollar.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  also surprised global markets this year when it\par engineered a sharp decline in the yuan. Last week, the yuan\par suffered its biggest-ever weekly decline of around 0.9 percent,\par capping off its largest monthly loss -- 1.4 percent -- in\par February.\par     While there is various speculation of the purposes of the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's latest move, some academics have criticised its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading, calling for freer convertibility.\par     "The essential method to curb hot money inflows and maintain\par financial stability is for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stop \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and let the yuan appreciate to\par proper levels once and for all," Yu Yongding, an influential\par researcher at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese Academy of Social Sciences\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said.\par     Yu, who was once also an academic advisor to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , made the written comments in response to an interview\par request by Reuters.\par             \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par  Item                        Current    Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1249     6.1257     0.01%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1159     6.1282     0.20%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   -0.15%                \par  Spot change ytd                                   1.87%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                35.33%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par  The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par  Instrument                 Current        Difference\par                                            from onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan         6.1123         0.06%\par           *                                \par  Offshore non-deliverable   6.1559         -0.50%\par  forwards               **                 \par  \par \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from Bloc's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - China's attack on yuan speculators risks backfiring\par  \par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opens liquidity front in hot money\par war \par      - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par      - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par     - China investors face bumpy ride as reform speculation\par intensifies \par     - CHINA MONEY - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  preparing market for more yuan\par volatility \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan is positive outlier compared with plunging emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money tracker: Hot money inflows slowed to a trickle\par in December 2013 GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior reflects yuan appreciation\par expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     \par \par  (Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-9T05:19:28.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140306ea36006em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
