\par\par \b \uc2 China Shares Down After Liquidity Withdrawal by PBOC; Electric Vehicle Stocks Lead -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,639 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 03:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0253 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares fall, extending Tuesday's 0.9% drop as investors keep cautious on lackluster outlook for domestic economy, say analysts. The Shanghai Composite Index drops 0.6% at 2040.00, and is tipped to find immediate support at 2000. "Investors are waiting to see whether Beijing will take measures to support economic growth," says Guo Feng, chief investment adviser with Northeast Securities, adding that the PBOC's liquidity withdrawal is also weighing on sentiment as it signals the PBOC's effort to avoid excess funds in the market. The PBOC is poised to drain a net 70 billion yuan this week compared with 160 billion yuan withdrawn last week, traders said Thursday. Electric vehicle manufacturers succumb to profit-taking; BYD (002594.SZ) falls 3.8% to CNY53.95 and Anhui Jianghuai Automobile (600418.SH) loses 4.7% to CNY9.46. Coal miners drop amid a slowing economic growth; Yanzhou Coal Mining (600188.SH) falls 2.9% to CNY6.37 and Shaanxi Coal Industry (601225.SH) loses 2.3% to CNY4.27. The Shenzhen Composite Index is down 1.3% at 1089.50. (amy.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0251 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/IDR is likely to test the 11,500 round-figure support soon on consistent inflows from foreign investors fueling demand for the rupiah. USD/IDR is now 11,525--a new four-month high--compared with its Wednesday close of 11,580. It's Asia's top-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year with a 5.1% gain. The rally may have been sparked by stronger-than-expected Australia economic data that has led to a return of risk taking in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are stronger after Australia posted a large trade surplus together with upbeat retail sales figures for February. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0251 GMT [Dow Jones] China yuan extend gains Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't show up in this week's spot trading after guiding the yuan to a 10-month-low Friday. The USD/CNY pair is at 6.1121 vs 6.1282 Wednesday close, after the central parity is set at 6.1249 vs 6.1257 Wednesday. "The pair may see a resistance at around 6.1000 psychological level and I expect it to range between 6.1000 and 6.1600 in the coming sessions," says a Shanghai-based foreign bank trader, adding the yuan's increased two-way volatility is in line with the PBOC's expectations. Offshore, one-year USD/CNY NDFs are down at 6.1580/6.1605 from 6.1630/6.1655 late Wednesday. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0245 GMT [Dow Jones] Philippine stocks lead Southeast Asia higher early Thursday. The benchmark PSEi gains 0.9% to 6516.4, with \uc2 Petron Corp\uc2 . (PCOR.PH)and \uc2 LT Group Inc\uc2 . (LTG.PH) performing strongly, up 4.3% and 3.7% respectively. In other markets, Indonesia's JSX and Singapore's FTSE Straits Times gain 0.2% each, while Malaysia's KLCI remains flat. "It's a light day for Asian data today. The most important event will be the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting where the overnight policy rate is expected to remain unchanged at 3.0%," UOB says in a note. Most markets continue on a strengthening trend, led by stock-pickers buying into the region's solid economic growth prospects. (jake.watts@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0234 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/INR may head lower toward the floor of its six-month range between 60.83 and 63.90, DBS says, after data showed India's current account deficit narrowed to less than 1% of GDP in the October-December 2013 quarter. "In USD terms, the USD4.2 billion posted during this quarter was a five-year low," the bank says. DBS notes the rupee first stabilized when the country's current account deficit narrowed to less than 2% of GDP in the June-September quarter. "With the balance of payments more stable, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now directing efforts to rein in inflation, the other symptom of macroeconomic imbalances. Success here will bring down both the 10-year bond yield and USD/INR and lift Sensex stocks," DBS says. Spot USD/INR was recently at 61.75. (jerry.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0158 GMT [Dow Jones] Malaysia shares are slightly up with the benchmark KLCI eking out a 0.1% gain at 1830.48 after Wall Street's lackluster overnight performance. Kenanga Research says the KLCI is still rangebound within a 1813-1833 range in the near term; "While the index-linked counters are likely to continue to consolidate, we believe that the rotational play on the small cap and penny stocks is likely to continue," the house adds. Gainers outnumber losers 247 to 156 with 545 million shares changing hands. Among the most active index stocks, Tenaga Nasional (5347.KU) is flat at MYR11.96, \uc2 Axiata Group\uc2  (6888.KU) up 0.2% at MYR6.55 and MISC (3816.KU) is up 2.8% at MYR6.53. (jason.ng@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [Dow Jones] Tocom rubber futures are lower amid profit-taking after strong gains Wednesday as high stockpiles at Qingdao weigh amid the low-production season. A broker in Kuala Lumpur says market perception is that demand is not strong enough to digest the stockpiles, which is keeping the sentiment weak. Benchmark August Tocom rubber trades Y1.9 lower at Y231.6/kg. (huileng.tan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [Dow Jones] The yuan is advancing for a third day--rising to 6.1120 from a Wednesday closing of 6.1282 as traders are drawn into betting on the yuan again after \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2 's PBOC appears to have stopped \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market since Tuesday. USD/CNY may next fall toward 6.1008 where the base of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel lies. The yuan gained 0.4% Wednesday before closing at 6.1282 and has reversed almost half of the losses engineered by the \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The increasing price fluctuation this week demonstrates the two-way volatility the Chinese authorities have been trying to encourage in the spot market. There is likely to be caution in holding large yuan bets after PBOC Vice Gov. Yi Gang says the fall of the yuan is normal and the bank will increase yuan flexibility in the future. USD/CNY is now 6.1120 versus its Wednesday close of 6.1282. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0149 GMT [Dow Jones] Australia's S&P/ASX 200 is on track to reach 6000 by year end says Equity Trustees CIO, George Boubouras. "I was very happy with the reporting season, given that earnings were more broad-based than we've seen for many years," he says. "It's still fragile going forward, in terms of revenue, but companies are well positioned to benefit from economic recovery." Mr. Boubouras says a 6000 target this year is "very achievable", assuming full-year earnings reports in August confirm the EPS growth projected in the interim earnings period. On Ukraine, Mr. Boubouras expects more jitters in coming months, but "from my perspective as a fund manager, I like short-term geopolitical shocks that create buying opportunities in quality companies." Index is last down 0.1% at 5440.0. (david.rogers@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0147 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY is moderately higher, driven by the JPY sales against the AUD following robust Australian retail sales and trade data, says a senior dealer at a Japanese bank. The situation in Ukraine is still "unsettling and unpredictable", but that hasn't led to a risk reduction globally, he says. Following a halt to slides in emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Yuan and the Rouble, some traders are shifting their attention to major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the U.S. February jobs report due Friday. The USD/JPY is at 102.51 compared with its earlier low of 102.27. Offers from exporters are lining up above 102.60. (tatsuo.ito@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0148 GMT [Dow Jones] The charts suggest USD/MYR is likely on its way lower implying the ringgit will rally toward 3.2530 as the daily Bollinger downtrend channel continues to drag the U.S. dollar down. The Malaysia \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meets to discuss its monetary policy Thursday and will announce its decision at 1000 GMT. Most analysts expect no change to the benchmark interest rate because inflation remains under control. A Thursday USD/MYR close below 3.2570--the base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support zone and, therefore, an important technical floor--may see the ringgit rally more vigorously toward 3.1970 where the weekly Ichimoku Cloud support awaits. USD/MYR is now 3.2690 versus its Wednesday close of 3.2695. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 0146 GMT [Dow Jones] After a weak opening the South Korea won is experiencing a bout of strength triggered by upbeat Australia economic data. USD/KRW opened at 1,071.5 but has dropped to the 1,068.0 base of the daily Ichimoku Cloud support and may fall further on a daily close below this important technical support. The surprisingly strong Australia trade surplus and retail-sales figures for February has whet investors' risk appetite. Asian emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are mostly stronger via proxy effect after the Australia data Thursday morning. On a Thursday close below 1,068 USD/KRW could head for the daily Bollinger downtrend channel that begins at 1,065. USD/KRW is now 1,068.5 versus its Wednesday close of 1,070.9. (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 05, 2014 21:53 ET (02:53 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140306ea36000fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
