\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan in biggest rise since 2012 as annual parliament opens\b0\par\par\uc2 972 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 11:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan rises 0.24 pct, biggest one-day gain since Dec 2012\par     * Big gain comes on opening day of annual parliament session\par     * State banks buy fewer dollars - traders\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  aims to bridge midpoint/spot yuan gap\par \par  (Updates to close)\par     By Gabriel Wildau and Lu Jianxin\par     SHANGHAI, March 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan had its best day\par since late 2012 on Wednesday, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to\par reduce its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, freeing the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par reverse a large chunk of its losses since mid-January.\par     Dollar purchases by state banks -- a sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 designed to weaken the yuan --\par appeared to subside this week, traders said.\par     The gain coincided with the opening session of an annual\par parliament meeting, leading some traders to speculate the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par may have permitted the yuan to appreciate in a show of strength.\par  \par     Spot yuan closed at 6.1282 per dollar, or 0.24\par percent stronger than Tuesday's close and the largest one-day\par gain since Dec. 24. \par     The strengthening spot rate contrasted with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's midpoint, which was fixed at 6.1257 on Wednesday, 0.03\par percent weaker than Tuesday and at the weakest level in three\par months for a second straight day.\par     "Fewer dollar purchases by state banks permitted the yuan to\par rise slightly in line with a lingering oversupply of dollars in\par the market," said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "That means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be happy with the yuan's current\par value," he said. \par     The trader noted that the softer midpoint likely was not a\par signal that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  intends to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but rather\par wants to let the spot rate move closer to the fixing, ahead of\par possible policy reforms to the midpoint mechanism.\par     Unless there's another surprise from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par yuan is likely to move within a 400-pip range around 6.15\par against the dollar, traders said.\par     In the longer term, however, the world's second-largest\par economy still faces heavy capital inflows under both the current\par account and capital accounts -- which means the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par still has potential to appreciate gradually, traders said.\par   \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised global markets last month when it\par engineered a sharp decline in the yuan. Last week, the yuan\par suffered its biggest-ever weekly decline of around 0.9 percent,\par capping off its largest monthly loss -- 1.4 percent -- in\par February.\par     Traders reported that onshore and offshore speculators had\par built up large long yuan positions earlier this year, after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market by letting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise\par 2.9 percent in 2013. That far exceeded initial market\par expectations for an appreciation of only 1 percent.\par     But following the PBOC-engineered depreciation, there were\par signs that companies have become less aggressive in betting on\par the yuan's appreciation, the traders said. \par     Many economists have predicted the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may also be testing\par waters for further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reforms, such as a widening of the\par yuan/dollar trading band to encourage more two-way trading.\par     "Conditions for exchange-rate reforms are relatively good.\par We see a rare two-way fluctuation in exchange rate, which could\par be a prelude to reforms," Li Daokui, an academic and former \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par adviser told reporters in Beijing on Wednesday.\par     "The floating band of yuan exchange rate could be expanded\par appropriately. And the process of capital-account convertibility\par could be quickened," Li said on the sidelines of the parliament\par meeting. \par     Still, many traders believe the current band of 1 percent up\par or down is sufficient for trading and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no need to\par rush to change it.\par     In particular, the band limits trading prices against the\par same day's midpoint, not the previous day's closing price, so\par even with a wider band, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could continue to\par control the exchange rate by fixing its midpoint further from\par the spot rate, traders say.\par             \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par      \par  Item                       Current      Previous   Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1257       6.1236       -0.03\par  Spot yuan                  6.1282       6.1430       +0.24\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.19                    \par  (pct)                                              \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.21\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 +35.06\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par  The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par         \par  Instrument                   Current      Difference from\par                                            onshore (pct)\par  Offshore spot yuan           6.1250       +0.05\par  Offshore non-deliverable     6.1623       -0.59\par  forwards                                  \par  \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from Bloc's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - China's attack on yuan speculators risks backfiring\par  \par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opens liquidity front in hot money\par war \par      - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par      - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par     - China investors face bumpy ride as reform speculation\par intensifies \par     - CHINA MONEY - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  preparing market for more yuan\par volatility \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan is positive outlier compared with plunging emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money tracker: Hot money inflows slowed to a trickle\par in December 2013 GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior reflects yuan appreciation\par expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     \par \par  (Editing by Richard Borsuk)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-8T10:21:05.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140305ea35008cq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
