\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2 's yuan edges up as \uc2 PBOC\uc2  reduces  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 914 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 06:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * State banks buy fewer dollars - traders\par     * But \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  still aims to bridge midpoint/spot yuan gap\par     * Yuan may move within 400 pips around 6.15 for now -\par traders\par     * But capital inflows may still mean yuan rise in long run\par \par     By Lu Jianxin and Gabriel Wildau\par     SHANGHAI, March 5 (Reuters) - China's yuan firmed slightly\par against the dollar on Wednesday as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appeared to\par reduce its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market, having engineered a\par sudden depreciation of the yuan since last month, traders said.\par     Dollar purchases by state banks -- a sign of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (PBOC) -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 appeared to subside this\par week, traders said.\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.1371 per dollar at midday,\par 0.1 percent stronger than Tuesday's close.\par     The strengthening spot rate contrasted with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's midpoint, which was fixed at 6.1257 on Wednesday, 0.03\par percent weaker than Tuesday and at the weakest level in three\par months for a second day in a row.\par     "Fewer dollar purchases by state banks permitted the yuan to\par rise slightly in line with a lingering oversupply of dollars in\par the market," said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "That means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be happy with the yuan's current\par value," he said. "As for the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  setting another three-month\par low midpoint, it appears the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hopes to eventually\par bring its base rate closer to the spot rate."\par     Absent another surprise from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the yuan is\par likely to move within a 400-pip range around 6.15 against the\par dollar, traders said.\par     In the longer term, however, the world's second-largest\par economy still faces heavy capital inflows under both the current\par account and capital accounts, which means the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par still has potential to appreciate gradually, traders said.\par   \par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised global markets last month when it\par engineered a sharp decline in the yuan. Last week, the yuan\par suffered its biggest-ever weekly decline of around 0.9 percent,\par capping off its largest monthly loss - 1.4 percent - in\par February.\par     Traders reported that onshore and offshore speculators had\par built up large long yuan positions earlier this year, after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market by letting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise\par 2.9 percent in 2013. That far exceeded initial market\par expectations for an appreciation of only 1 percent.\par     But they said there were signs companies have become less\par aggressive in betting on the yuan's appreciation more recently\par after the PBOC-engineered depreciation.\par     Many economists have predicted the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may also be testing\par waters for further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reforms, such as a widening of the\par yuan/dollar trading band to encourage more two-way trading.\par     "Conditions for exchange-rate reforms are relatively good.\par We see a rare two-way fluctuation in exchange rate, which could\par be a prelude to reforms," Li Daokui, an academic and former \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par adviser told reporters in Beijing on Wednesday.\par     "The floating band of yuan exchange rate could be expanded\par appropriately. And the process of capital-account convertibility\par could be quickened," he said on the sidelines of the opening\par session of China's annual parliamentary meeting. \par     Still, many traders believe the current band of 1 percent up\par or down is sufficient for trading and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  has no need to\par rush to change it.\par     In particular, the band limits trading prices against the\par same day's midpoint, not the previous day's closing price, so\par even with a wider band, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could continue to\par control the exchange rate by fixing its midpoint further from\par the spot rate, traders say.\par             \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par      \par  Item                       Current      Previous   Change (pct)\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint              6.1257       6.1236       -0.03\par  Spot yuan                  6.1371       6.1430       +0.10\par  Divergence from midpoint*  0.19                    \par  (pct)                                              \par  Spot change ytd                                    -1.36\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                 +34.86\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par  The offshore yuan market at a glance:    