\par\par \b \uc2 China's yuan slips in line with \uc2 PBOC\uc2  midpoint, near-term trend unclear\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 06:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets midpoint at three-month low\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trade lessens - traders\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may keep yuan around 6.15 for now\par     * Midpoint will be crucial benchmark to watch\par \par     By Lu Jianxin and Pete Sweeney\par     SHANGHAI, March 4 (Reuters) - China's yuan slipped against\par the dollar on Tuesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its official\par midpoint at a three-month low, suggesting it is not yet ready to\par release the recent pressure on the yuan, traders said.\par     Traders said there were signs companies have become less\par aggressive in betting on the yuan's appreciation.\par     "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  appears to be happy with a pause of the sharp yuan\par depreciation, possibly believing the market has learned a\par lesson," said a trader at a Chinese commercial bank in Shanghai.\par     "While we can never be certain of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's intention, the\par yuan's movements so far this week appears to hint that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may let the yuan move around 6.15 for now."\par     On the day, dollar purchases by state banks -- a sign the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trading -- appeared to\par have subsided, traders said.\par     Spot yuan stood at 6.1499 per dollar at midday,\par down 0.06 percent from Monday's close after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  fixed the\par yuan's midpoint at 6.1190, down 0.08 percent from the previous\par day. It also marked the official base rate's weakest level since\par Dec. 5, 2013.\par     Traders said the yuan's daily limit of 1 percent in either\par direction of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's base rate implied that spot yuan had\par little room to move far away from its recent low of 6.1808, its\par nearly one-year trough hit last Friday.\par     But they said the near-term trend remained unclear because\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could change its stance at any time.\par     "Judging from Tuesday's midpoint, we can safely say the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par has no intention to let the yuan depreciate much in the near\par term," said a trader at a European bank in Shanghai.\par     "But if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  lets the midpoint weaken beyond 6.13 or\par even more, the market should be vigilant that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par may be engineering another round of yuan depreciation."\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised global markets since last month when it\par began engineering a sharp decline in the yuan.  Last week, the\par yuan suffered its biggest-ever weekly decline of around 0.9\par percent, capping off its largest monthly loss - 1.4 percent - in\par February.\par     Traders reported that onshore and offshore speculators had\par built up large long positions on the yuan earlier this year\par after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surprised the market by letting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise 2.9 percent in 2013. That far exceeded initial\par market expectations for an appreciation of only 1 percent.\par      Repeated government pledges to quicken the pace of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reform even as the yuan rallied relentlessly since  July 2012,\par were interpreted by many investors as a sign of  more\par appreciation to come, sparking rampant speculation.\par     In the longer term, however, the world's second-largest\par economy is still under pressure from heavy capital inflows both\par under the current account and the capital account, and the\par Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has thus limited room to depreciate, traders\par said.  \par     \par  The onshore spot yuan market at a glance: \par     \par  Item                        Current      Previous   Change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  midpoint               6.1236       6.1190     -0.08%\par  Spot yuan                   6.1499       6.1462     -0.06%\par  Divergence from midpoint*   0.43%                   \par  Spot change ytd                                     1.56%\par  Spot change since 2005 revaluation                  34.58%\par  \par *Divergence of the dollar/yuan exchange rate. Negative number\par indicates that spot yuan is trading stronger than the midpoint.\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China (PBOC) \f28 \uc2 \f2 allows the exchange rate to\par rise or fall 1 percent from official midpoint rate it sets each\par morning.\par \par  The offshore yuan market at a glance:    \par     \par  Instrument                   Current      Difference from\par                                            onshore\par  Offshore spot yuan           6.1287       0.35%\par  Offshore non-deliverable     6.1570       -0.54%\par  forwards                                  \par     \par *Premium for offshore spot over onshore \par **Figure reflects difference from \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's official midpoint,\par since non-deliverable forwards are settled against the midpoint.\par . \par     \par     >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     RECENT DEVELOPMENTS\par     - China's attack on yuan speculators risks backfiring\par  \par     - \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opens liquidity front in hot money\par war \par      - New quotas rekindle debate over dim sum market's future\par  \par      - Flood of offshore yuan bonds may spark higher yields\par  \par     - China investors face bumpy ride as reform speculation\par intensifies \par     - CHINA MONEY - \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  preparing market for more yuan\par volatility \par         \par     KEY DATA POINTS\par     - Yuan is positive outlier compared with plunging emerging\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/cyx46v}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Hot money tracker: Hot money inflows slowed to a trickle\par in December 2013 GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/saz74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/saz74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - China's trade surpluses mainly driven by weak imports\par rather than strong exports. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/qav68s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/qav68s}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Corporate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  behavior reflects yuan appreciation\par expectations. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/tyx74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     - Despite relatively stable dollar/yuan exchange rate, the\par yuan is appreciating on a trade-weighted basis. GRAPHIC: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/sed74t"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/sed74t}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     \par     \par    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\par     \par \par  (Editing by Shri Navaratnam)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-3-7T05:42:07.000Z   