\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 China \highlight\uc2  Yuan Rises; No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  From PBOC\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par                                   Vs Parity  Previous \par USD/CNY Central Parity   6.1236               6.1190 \par USD/CNY OTC 0830 GMT     6.1430    -0.32%     6.1462 \par             High         6.1595    -0.59% \par             Low          6.1426    -0.31% \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SHANGHAI--China's yuan advanced against the U.S. dollar late Tuesday as investors sold the safe-haven dollar in the absence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and also after a report indicating Russian President Vladimir Putin ordered a halt to military exercises.\f28 \par \par \uc2 On the over-the-counter market the dollar was at 6.1430 yuan around 0830 GMT compared with Monday's close at 6.1462 yuan. It traded between 6.1426 yuan and 6.1595 yuan.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate at 6.1236, higher than Monday's 6.1190, following dollar strength overseas. But traders were more interested in the PBOC \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market after it had surprisingly pushed the yuan to a 10-month low Friday.\par \par \uc2 Recent yuan volatility is normal, PBOC Gov. \uc2 Zhou Xiaochuan\uc2  said according to the official \uc2 Xinhua News Agency\uc2  Tuesday. He will elaborate at a news briefing soon. But investors worry the bank may push the yuan even weaker in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would want the onshore and offshore yuan to weaken to around 6.20 to squeeze out the structure products and bets on a steady yuan rise," a Shanghai-based local bank trader said.\par \par \uc2 The yuan began sliding against the dollar recently after a long period of gradual appreciation. After hitting a record 6.0406 against the dollar in January it has lost 1.7%.\par \par \uc2 Offshore, one-year dollar/yuan nondeliverable forward contracts were at 6.1580/6.1605 from 6.1570/6.1613 late Monday implying a 0.1% fall by the yuan over the next year.\par \par \uc2 In the offshore yuan market in Hong Kong, where the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats freely, the dollar was at CNY6.1265, higher than CNY6.1217 late Monday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Wynne Wang at wynne.wang@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 March 04, 2014 04:01 ET (09:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140304ea34000tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
