\par\par \b \uc2 Yuan Tanks Again; Hits 9-Month Low of 6.1630 -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2014\par 04:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 0309 GMT [Dow Jones] China's yuan falls sharply again, after two days of relative calm, to hit a new 9-month trough of 6.1630 to the U.S. dollar. The move was likely triggered by another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 People's Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 China\b0 \highlight\uc2  to flush out speculative long-yuan positions. The yuan's fall accelerated as bank clients' stop-loss orders below 6.1500 were activated to cut losses for punters who are still holding on to the yuan. The \uc2 Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has since last week been tightening the screws on speculators who have been betting on the yuan to appreciate sharply once the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is fully liberalized. The recent attempt to weaken the yuan has resulted in a 2.0% drop in its value since Feb. 19 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began; last year, the yuan rallied 3.0%.\par \par \uc2  The PBOC's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been classified by most market participants as a move to introduce greater two-way volatility for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the daily trading band is widened from its current 1.0% range.\par \par \uc2 Spot USD/CNY is now 6.1530 from its Thursday close of 6.1284. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 27, 2014 22:09 ET (03:09 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140228ea2s000vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\png