\par\par \b \uc2 CANADA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  DEBT-C$ slips as commodity prices weaken on China worries\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2014\par 22:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Canadian dollar at C$1.1086 or 90.20 U.S. cents\par     * Bond prices higher across the maturity curve\par \par \par     By Leah Schnurr and Alastair Sharp\par     TORONTO, Feb 25 (Reuters) - The Canadian dollar weakened\par against the U.S. dollar on Tuesday, pulling back as the biggest\par drop since October 2011 in the Chinese yuan put a scare into\par commodity-related \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the loonie.\par     The Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had gained in the prior session after\par several weak days late last week, but fell with other\par resource-linked \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  including the Australian and New\par Zealand dollars as strategists feared what the yuan move means\par for global growth.\par     Economists and traders suspect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 China\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to add volatility to the yuan in preparation for\par reform. The yuan's drop extended its fall in the past week to\par slightly over 1 percent. \par     The Canadian dollar can be sensitive to developments in\par China, a major consumer of commodities. \par     "The tone of the day was defensive and that came after the\par devaluation in the Chinese yuan, the largest in two years," said\par Jack Spitz, managing director of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at National\par Bank Financial.\par     The Canadian dollar had received a boost after Bank of\par Canada Governor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Stephen Poloz\f28 \uc2 \f2  said over the weekend that two\par months of stronger domestic inflation has made the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par feel a little more comfortable.\par     The comments reduced some of the speculation that the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could sound more dovish at its next meeting in\par March, and had helped lift the loonie on Monday.\par     "Today we're just giving a little bit of it back, but so far\par it's been very, very quiet in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets," said Camilla Sutton,\par chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Scotiabank in Toronto.\par     The comments, along with last week's stronger-than-expected\par rise in the inflation rate, "would suggest a pretty neutral\par environment for the Canadian dollar," said Sutton.\par     That likely means the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is somewhat stuck in a range\par along the lines of where it traded in February between C$1.0911\par and C$1.1224, she said.\par     The Canadian dollar ended the session at C$1.1086\par to the greenback, or 90.20 U.S. cents, weaker than Monday's\par close of C$1.1067, or 90.36 U.S. cents.\par     With a light economic calendar this week, the Canadian\par dollar won't have much in the way of domestic catalysts until a\par report on fourth-quarter gross domestic product is released on\par Friday.\par     Growth is forecast to slip to a 2.5 percent annualized rate,\par though the report may carry less weight than usual as harsh\par winter weather in parts of Canada in December is expected to\par have temporarily disrupted activity.\par     National's Spitz said that with low expectations comes a\par greater chance of a loonie bounce on the data.\par     "I think the market is pricing in soft (domestic) data and\par so the surprise would be an upside surprise," he said. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Canadian government\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond prices were higher across the\par maturity curve, with the two-year up half a Canadian\par cent to yield 1.024 percent and the benchmark 10-year\par  up 36 Canadian cents to yield 2.482 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-2-28T21:51:12.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140225ea2p00h4t\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (china near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw)and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\b